;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; name: battlefront-city.gc
;; name in dgo: battlefront-city
;; dgos: CWI

#|
  Battlefront mod -- the part of a battle that needs Haven City's own types (attack controller,
  faction manager, the guards' grenade). Linked with CWI, so it only exists while Haven City is
  loaded; the GAME code (pc/features/battlefront/) reaches it through `*bf-city-hook*` and
  `*bf-city-grenade*`, which this file sets at link time, and calls them only while ctywide is
  active (a fresh link of this file).

  Hatred: the attack controller (wascity/mission-squad-control.gc) gives each unit the target of
  best score, its hatred times a distance factor times a crowd factor, twice for the one it has, and
  looks again now and then. During a battle every pair of foes takes the battle's own hatreds
  (`bf-city-apply-hatred`): the nearest foe first (the score falls to 0 at 120 m), kept until it
  dies (no look again), the player twice as hated as a unit by the other side and not at all by his
  own. The changed entries are saved first and written back when the battle ends.

  Battle points: the bases and a control point in each district (battlefront-h.gc
  `*bf-point-defs*`); the units take their lanes toward the nearest point their side holds, to
  defend it, or toward the nearest it does not (`bf-city-steer`, `bf-city-choose-branch`); each side's troop transports (bf-transport.gc) bring
  its units to the points it holds in the sections loaded, the nearest the player first
  (`bf-city-transports`): during a fight the traffic wakes none of the battle's units by itself
  (battlefront-h.gc `bf-wake-count`). The battlefield is the whole city: no force field.

  No Spargus citizen fights here: wastelanders brought into Haven City by the traffic engine froze
  or crashed the game within minutes (in the background collision query
  fill-bg-using-line-sphere-new, seen in two of two ten-minute battles; none in a battle without
  them). The Spargus Citizen class is gone too: nothing of the wastelanders loads in Haven City.
|#

;; DECOMP BEGINS

;; attack-controller types (city-target-type) of a battle: the player (the controller's
;; target-attacker), the Freedom League's guards (3 to 5: tazer, rifle, grenade; the blue jetpacks
;; register as rifle guards), the Krimzon Guard's units (9 to 12: roboguard, turret, spydroid, giant;
;; the red guards register as roboguards)
(defconstant BF_CTT_JAK 0)
(define *bf-ctt* (new 'static 'array int32 8 0 3 4 5 9 10 11 12))

(defconstant BF_HATE_REACH (meters 100))   ;; a foe beyond this scores 0: never chosen (at 50 m the armies
                                           ;; passed each other: 8 losses in 6 minutes)
(defconstant BF_HATE_LOST (meters 150))    ;; a unit whose foe got this far looks again
(defconstant BF_HATE_PLAYER (meters 50))   ;; the other side turns onto the player this close
;; Every unit of a battle walks and runs faster than the game's (`bf-city-unit-pace`): its walk and
;; run speeds times its kind's `*bf-unit-pace*`, the ground its walk and run clips cover the stock
;; one, so its legs step at its speed (round 35, the author's wish: until then that ground was
;; scaled too, the legs at the stock cadence slid over the ground) (citizen-travel-anim plays them at its speed over that ground), the
;; player's guard's (battlefront-player.gc BF_CLASS_PACE). The guards' run speed alone raised to
;; 18 m/s played their run clip 1.5 times as fast as the player's; the nav control's speed-scale
;; instead left the spiders at 8 m/s and the guards at 16 (round 22's runs).
;; Each kind's pace against the stock one, in `bf-unit-kind` order: guard, jetpack, robotguard on
;; foot, spider. 1.5 for all until round 33; then the author's wish: guards 1.4 times as fast as
;; that, robotguards on foot 2 times, spiders 1.6 times (2.1, 3.0 and 2.4 times the stock); round
;; 35, the guards a little slower, 1.9; round 36, slower again, 1.6 (their legs keep pace, their
;; clip grounds the stock ones); round 49, the stock pace, 1.0: at 1.6 their walk and run clips
;; played 1.6 times as fast and looked sped up (the author's report); round 50, 1.6 again (the
;; author's wish: the speed of round 36, the clips calibrated, `*bf-unit-stride*`).
(define *bf-unit-pace* (new 'static 'array float 4 1.6 1.5 3.0 2.4))

;; The ground each kind's walk and run clips cover against the stock one, in `bf-unit-kind` order:
;; the clips play at the kind's pace over its stride (`*bf-unit-pace*` / this). The guards' 1.3
;; plays their clips 1.23 times as fast at 1.6 times the stock speed (1.6 times in round 36, which
;; looked sped up; a stride of 1.6 plays them at the stock cadence, the feet sliding, round 34's
;; complaint). Round 50.
(define *bf-unit-stride* (new 'static 'array float 4 1.3 1.0 1.0 1.0))

;; The stock walk speed, run speed, walk clip ground and run clip ground of each kind (`bf-unit-kind`:
;; guard.gc, flying-turret.gc, roboguard-city.gc, spydroid.gc init-enemy!), in units.
(define *bf-unit-stock-pace* (new 'static 'array float 16
                                  12288.0 49152.0 12288.0 34078.72
                                  102400.0 102400.0 8192.0 16384.0
                                  12288.0 49152.0 16384.0 26624.0
                                  16384.0 32768.0 8192.0 16384.0
                                  )
  )

;; A robotguard marching to a point farther than BF_ROLL_REACH rolls there as a ball (the author's
;; wish), until BF_ROLL_STOP from it (`bf-city-roll!`).
(defconstant BF_ROLL_REACH (meters 35))       ;; the stock robot rolls toward a foe this far (roboguard-city-method-235)
(defconstant BF_ROLL_STOP (meters 25))
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_KIND 2)                 ;; its index in `*bf-kinds*`
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_RUN_CLIP 11)            ;; roboguard-city-ag run, its stock anim-run
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_BALL_CLIP 13)           ;; roboguard-city-ag ball
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_ROLL_SPEED (meters 45)) ;; the stock roll's 20 m/s times BF_ROLL_SCALE (battlefront-h.gc; 30 m/s until round 33)
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_BALL_DIST 43690.0)      ;; ground a loop of the ball clip covers: the stock roll's pace
                                              ;; (roll-chase plays it at speed / 40960, the travel clip at
                                              ;; 16 speed / 15 dist)

(define-extern bf-marching? (function process symbol))

(defun bf-city-unit-pace ((proc process))
  "Unit PROC of the battle (a citizen) at its kind's pace (`*bf-unit-pace*`) times its kind's stock
   walk and run speeds, its clip grounds the stock ones times its kind's stride (`*bf-unit-stock-pace*`,
   `*bf-unit-stride*`): written each time, so a unit woken again (its init
   sets the stock values back) is paced within half a second. A robotguard not marching gets its
   stock run clip back (a march's roll gives it the ball, `bf-city-roll!`)."
  (let ((k (bf-unit-kind proc))
        (unit (the-as citizen proc))
        )
    (when (>= k 0)
      (let ((base (* 4 k))
            (pace (-> *bf-unit-pace* k))
            )
        (set! (-> unit speed-walk) (* pace (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* base)))
        (set! (-> unit speed-run) (* pace (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* (+ base 1))))
        (set! (-> unit dist-walk-anim) (* (-> *bf-unit-stride* k) (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* (+ base 2))))
        (set! (-> unit dist-run-anim) (* (-> *bf-unit-stride* k) (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* (+ base 3))))
        )
      (if (and (= k BF_ROBOT_KIND) (not (bf-marching? unit)))
          (set! (-> unit anim-run) BF_ROBOT_RUN_CLIP)
          )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defconstant BF_CONTEST_REACH (meters 350)) ;; a unit this close to a contested point goes to clear it or defend it (250 m until round 42)
(defconstant BF_ZONE_REACH (meters 60))     ;; a point's zone: the other side's units this close contest it
(defconstant BF_ENGAGE_REACH (meters 40))   ;; a unit with a foe this close stops its march to fight
(defconstant BF_THREAT_REACH (meters 150))  ;; a point's guards hold it while the other side's units come this close

;; Each side's units in each battle point's zone (BF_ZONE_REACH), counted twice a second from
;; `*bf-unit-dots*` (`bf-city-steer`): index BF_POINT_MAX side + point.
(define *bf-zone-near* (new 'static 'array int32 34)) ;; 2 BF_POINT_MAX

;; The same within BF_THREAT_REACH: a point's guards (`bf-post-point`) hold it while the other side's
;; units are this close, and go on to the next point once none is.
(define *bf-threat-near* (new 'static 'array int32 34)) ;; 2 BF_POINT_MAX

;; The units with a foe within BF_ENGAGE_REACH at the last retarget (`bf-city-retarget`): they fight
;; instead of marching (`bf-march-plan`). Stopped by a foe up to BF_HATE_REACH (100 m), the units
;; stood and the armies' pushes died away (7 and 14 losses in 10 minutes, no point fought over).
(deftype bf-engaged (structure)
  ((count  int32)
   (unit   handle 512)
   )
  )

(define *bf-engaged* (new 'static 'bf-engaged))

(defun bf-city-engaged? ((proc process))
  "#t when unit PROC had a foe within BF_ENGAGE_REACH at the last retarget (`*bf-engaged*`)."
  (let ((h (process->handle proc))
        (e *bf-engaged*)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> e count))
      (if (= (-> e unit i) h)
          (return #t)
          )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(deftype bf-city-saved (structure)
  "Stock hatred indices overwritten during a battle, to write back at its end, and the battle's
   two hatreds pushed into the controller's list."
  ((saved?         symbol)
   (hatred         uint8 64)   ;; entry (row i, column j) of *bf-ctt* at 8 i + j
   (unit-info      int32)      ;; index of the battle's hatred between units
   (player-info    int32)      ;; index of the battle's hatred of the player
   (vals-length    int32)      ;; the list's length once they were pushed, 0 none
   (faction-time   time-frame) ;; last re-application of the battle's faction commands
   (reinforce-time time-frame) ;; last look at the sides' troop transports (`bf-city-transports`)
   (retarget-time  time-frame) ;; last look at the units near the player (`bf-city-retarget`)
   )
  )

(define *bf-city-saved* (new 'static 'bf-city-saved))

(defun bf-city-hatred-slot ((row int) (col int))
  "Index of the (attacker ROW, target COL) entry of the attack controller's hatred table."
  (+ (* row (-> *cty-attack-controller* max-num-object-types)) col)
  )

(defun bf-city-controller? ()
  "#t when Haven City's attack controller exists (it is built at ctywide login)."
  (and *cty-attack-controller* (nonzero? *cty-attack-controller*))
  )

(defun bf-ctt-team ((ctt int))
  "Side of attack-controller type CTT in a battle: BF_TEAM_FF, BF_TEAM_KG, the player's for 0,
   BF_TEAM_NONE for any other."
  (cond
    ((= ctt BF_CTT_JAK) (-> *bf* team))
    ((and (>= ctt 3) (<= ctt 5)) BF_TEAM_FF)
    ((and (>= ctt 9) (<= ctt 12)) BF_TEAM_KG)
    (else BF_TEAM_NONE)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-push-hatreds ()
  "Push the battle's two hatreds into the controller's list when they are not there: at the first
   call, and after a death reset rebuilt the list (cty-attack-reset -> reset-hatred, then the stock
   init-attack-controller pushes its own again, 12 of 22). Both score the nearest foe first: 1 near,
   falling to 0 at BF_HATE_REACH (dist-scale 0), with no penalty for a crowd on it (attacker-scale 1),
   and keep it until it dies (chi1: no look again on the controller's timer). The player is twice
   as hated as a unit."
  (let ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*)
        (saved *bf-city-saved*)
        )
    (when (or (zero? (-> saved vals-length)) (!= (-> ctrl hatred-vals length) (-> saved vals-length)))
      (when (>= (- (-> ctrl hatred-vals allocated-length) (-> ctrl hatred-vals length)) 2)
        (dotimes (i 2)
          (let ((info (push-back-hatred ctrl)))
            (set! (-> info hatred) (if (zero? i) 0.5 1.0))
            (set! (-> info hatred-dist) BF_HATE_REACH)
            (set! (-> info max-consider-dist) BF_HATE_REACH)
            (set! (-> info dist-scale) 0.0)
            (set! (-> info attacker-scale) 1.0)
            (set! (-> info flags) (city-hatred-info-flag chi1))
            (if (zero? i)
                (set! (-> saved unit-info) (the-as int (-> info index)))
                (set! (-> saved player-info) (the-as int (-> info index)))
                )
            )
          )
        (set! (-> saved vals-length) (-> ctrl hatred-vals length))
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-apply-hatred ()
  "The battle's hatreds between every attacker and target type of *bf-ctt*: none between a side's
   own (the player's included), the battle's unit hatred between foes, its player hatred from the
   other side's units onto the player. The stock entries are saved the first time. Written on every
   call: a death reset rebuilds the stock table, and the writes are idempotent. Then no unit keeps
   the guards' anger at the player (a 'member-attacked from the player's shots gives a guard a
   hatred-map-callback onto him, guard.gc), so his own side never turns on him."
  (when (bf-city-controller?)
    (bf-city-push-hatreds)
    (let* ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*)
           (saved *bf-city-saved*)
           (table (-> ctrl hatred-indices))
           )
      (when (not (-> saved saved?))
        (dotimes (i 8)
          (dotimes (j 8)
            (set! (-> saved hatred (+ (* 8 i) j)) (-> table (bf-city-hatred-slot (-> *bf-ctt* i) (-> *bf-ctt* j))))
            )
          )
        (set! (-> saved saved?) #t)
        )
      (when (nonzero? (-> saved vals-length))
        (dotimes (i 8)
          (dotimes (j 8)
            (let ((row (-> *bf-ctt* i))
                  (col (-> *bf-ctt* j))
                  )
              (when (!= row BF_CTT_JAK)
                (set! (-> table (bf-city-hatred-slot row col))
                      (cond
                        ((= (bf-ctt-team row) (bf-ctt-team col)) 0)
                        ((= col BF_CTT_JAK) (-> saved player-info))
                        (else (-> saved unit-info))
                        )
                      )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
        (let ((info (-> ctrl attackers data i)))
          (if (>= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) 0)
              (set! (-> info hatred-map-callback) #f)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; A foe a wall hides from a unit is passed over this long (`bf-city-sees?`, `bf-city-foe-ok?`).
(defconstant BF_SIGHT_HOLD (seconds 3))
(defconstant BF_SIGHT_TRIES 3) ;; hidden foes a unit passes over in one look before it takes none
(defconstant BF_ROBOT_SIGHT (meters 50)) ;; a robotguard takes a foe this close at most

(deftype bf-sight (structure)
  "The foes walls hid from each attacker of Haven City's attack controller (4 slots for its
   attacker index), and when (`bf-city-hide!`); BLIND set when its last look found only hidden
   foes: it takes none until its next look (`bf-city-retarget`)."
  ((foe   handle     2048)
   (time  time-frame 2048)
   (next  int8       512)
   (blind int8       512)
   )
  )

(define *bf-sight* (new 'static 'bf-sight))

;; Foes a wall hid since the battle began, for the tests (docs/modding/current_mod/battlefront_smoke.gc).
(define *bf-sight-count* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0))

(defun bf-city-sees? ((me process-drawable) (foe process-drawable))
  "#t when no scenery stands between ME's eyes (1.6 m up) and FOE's middle (1.2 m up): a thin probe
   of the background along the line. Units took foes through the thick walls between the
   Industrial Zone and the Slums, and fired into them (the author's play)."
  (let ((cq (new 'stack-no-clear 'collide-query)))
    (vector-copy! (-> cq start-pos) (-> me root trans))
    (+! (-> cq start-pos y) (meters 1.6))
    (vector-! (-> cq move-dist) (-> foe root trans) (-> me root trans))
    (+! (-> cq move-dist y) (meters -0.4))
    (set! (-> cq radius) (meters 0.2))
    (set! (-> cq collide-with) (collide-spec backgnd))
    (set! (-> cq ignore-process0) #f)
    (set! (-> cq ignore-process1) #f)
    (set! (-> cq ignore-pat) (new 'static 'pat-surface :noentity #x1 :nojak #x1 :probe #x1 :noendlessfall #x1 :board #x1))
    (set! (-> cq action-mask) (collide-action solid))
    (< (fill-and-probe-using-line-sphere *collide-cache* cq) 0.0)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-hide! ((k int) (foe handle))
  "Attacker K (its index in the controller) cannot see FOE: passed over for BF_SIGHT_HOLD."
  (when (and (>= k 0) (< k 512))
    (let ((slot (+ (* 4 k) (-> *bf-sight* next k))))
      (set! (-> *bf-sight* foe slot) foe)
      (set-time! (-> *bf-sight* time slot))
      (set! (-> *bf-sight* next k) (logand (+ (-> *bf-sight* next k) 1) 3))
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-foe-ok? ((me process) (foe city-attacker-info))
  "The battle's units' attacker callback (mission-squad-control-method-13 asks it of each foe it
   scores): none while it is blind (its last look found only foes behind walls), no foe a wall hid
   from it in the last BF_SIGHT_HOLD (`bf-city-hide!`), and for a
   robotguard none beyond BF_ROBOT_SIGHT (with the battle's 100 m sight the robotguards stood in
   'hostile-stand for minutes, 400 to 700 m from their point, on a foe they never reached). #f
   drops the foe, anything else keeps it. Every unit fights the foes it meets on its way to its
   point, then goes on (round 45, the author's wish; round 44 let 40 % pass them by)."
  (let ((p (handle->process (-> foe proc)))
        (info (if (and me (type? me citizen))
                  (-> (the-as citizen me) attacker-info)
                  )
              )
        (ok? (and me #t))
        )
    (when (and info (nonzero? info))
      (let ((k (-> info self-index)))
        (when (and (>= k 0) (< k 512))
          (if (nonzero? (-> *bf-sight* blind k))
              (set! ok? #f)
              )
          (dotimes (j 4)
            (if (and (= (-> *bf-sight* foe (+ (* 4 k) j)) (-> foe proc))
                     (not (time-elapsed? (-> *bf-sight* time (+ (* 4 k) j)) BF_SIGHT_HOLD))
                     )
                (set! ok? #f)
                )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (the-as int (and ok?
                     p
                     (type? p process-drawable)
                     (or (!= (-> me type symbol) 'roboguard-city)
                         (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> (the-as process-drawable p) root trans)
                                                       (-> (the-as process-drawable me) root trans)
                                                       )
                            BF_ROBOT_SIGHT
                            )
                         )
                     )
            )
    )
  )

;; The champions (round 49: the Krimzon Guard's; round 53: the Freedom League's), defined further down
(define-extern *bf-city-boss-info* city-attacker-info)
(define-extern *bf-city-boss-info-ff* city-attacker-info)
;; Spargus's precursor artifact (round 54), defined further down
(define-extern *bf-city-artifact-info* city-attacker-info)
(define-extern bf-city-artifact-pull! (function mission-squad-control city-attacker-info vector none))
(define-extern bf-city-boss-pull! (function mission-squad-control city-attacker-info city-attacker-info vector int none))
(define-extern bf-city-set-foe! (function mission-squad-control city-attacker-info int none))

(defun bf-city-retarget ()
  "Twice a second every unit of the battle looks again for a target (mission-squad-control-method-13,
   the controller's own choice: the battle's hatred scores a foe by its distance, 0 beyond
   BF_HATE_REACH, and its current foe twice): the units attack what they see, a foe near enough
   instead of one far away, and a unit with no foe that near goes on to its point. A foe a wall
   hides from the unit (`bf-city-sees?`) is passed over (`bf-city-hide!`), another one picked; after
   BF_SIGHT_TRIES hidden ones the unit takes none until its next look and goes on to its point (in
   the author's play, units in the Industrial Zone fired into a thick wall at foes in the Slums
   behind it, a second foe as hidden as the first). A unit of the other side within BF_HATE_PLAYER of the player, its foe
   farther than him, turns onto him (the player's hatred); a unit of the player's side never keeps
   him as its foe."
  (set! (-> *bf-engaged* count) 0)
  (when (and (bf-city-controller?) *target* (not (focus-test? *target* dead)))
    (let* ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*)
           (jak (-> ctrl target-attacker self-index))
           (here (-> *target* control trans))
           )
      (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
        (let ((info (-> ctrl attackers data i)))
          (when (and (logtest? (-> info flags) (city-attacker-info-flag cai0))
                     (!= i jak)
                     (>= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) 0)
                     )
            ;; a new look: the unit sees again (`bf-city-foe-ok?`)
            (if (< i 512)
                (set! (-> *bf-sight* blind i) 0)
                )
            (let* ((pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data i pos))
                   (foe (-> info enemy-index))
                   (foe-dist (if (>= foe 0)
                                 (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data foe pos))
                                 BF_HATE_LOST
                                 )
                             )
                   (jak-dist (vector-vector-xz-distance pos here))
                   )
              (if (or (and (!= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) (-> *bf* team))
                           (!= foe jak)
                           (< jak-dist BF_HATE_PLAYER)
                           (< jak-dist foe-dist)
                           )
                      ;; the others too, unless on the player: each takes the foe it sees best now
                      (!= foe jak)
                      (and (>= foe 0) (< BF_HATE_LOST foe-dist))
                      ;; a unit of his own side on the player: a target taken before the battle's
                      ;; hatreds (the stock ones, while the zone loaded) is kept until it dies (seen in
                      ;; game: a red guard and a red jetpack aiming at a Krimzon Guard player)
                      (and (= foe jak) (= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) (-> *bf* team)))
                      )
                  (mission-squad-control-method-13 ctrl info)
                  )
              ;; a foe behind a wall: passed over, another one picked (`bf-city-foe-ok?`), up to
              ;; BF_SIGHT_TRIES; then none until the next look
              (let ((tries 0))
                (while (and (< tries BF_SIGHT_TRIES) (>= (-> info enemy-index) 0))
                  (let ((me (handle->process (-> info proc)))
                        (them (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data (-> info enemy-index) proc)))
                        )
                    (cond
                      ((and me them (type? me process-drawable) (type? them process-drawable)
                            (not (bf-city-sees? (the-as process-drawable me) (the-as process-drawable them)))
                            )
                       (bf-city-hide! i (-> ctrl attackers data (-> info enemy-index) proc))
                       (+! (-> *bf-sight-count* 0) 1)
                       (+! tries 1)
                       ;; none left in sight: blind until the next look, unless it is in the middle
                       ;; of an attack (the stock's lock-focus); its foe gone then, the game crashed
                       ;; twice in three runs
                       (if (and (= tries BF_SIGHT_TRIES) (< i 512) (type? me enemy)
                                (not (logtest? (-> (the-as enemy me) enemy-flags) (enemy-flag lock-focus)))
                                )
                           (set! (-> *bf-sight* blind i) 1)
                           )
                       (mission-squad-control-method-13 ctrl info)
                       )
                      (else
                        (set! tries BF_SIGHT_TRIES)
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              ;; a side's champion (round 49: the Krimzon Guard's; round 53: the Freedom League's
              ;; too): a unit of the other side within BF_ENGAGE_REACH of him, nearer him than its
              ;; foe, turns onto him. The battle's hatred keeps a unit on its foe until it dies
              ;; (chi1), so the units fighting around him never picked him (0 in 90 s)
              (bf-city-boss-pull! ctrl info *bf-city-boss-info* pos BF_TEAM_FF)
              (bf-city-boss-pull! ctrl info *bf-city-boss-info-ff* pos BF_TEAM_KG)
              ;; Spargus's precursor artifact (round 54): the Krimzon Guard's units near it attack it
              (bf-city-artifact-pull! ctrl info pos)
              ;; a foe in sight now: the unit fights it, no march (`bf-march-plan`)
              (let ((nf (-> info enemy-index)))
                (when (and (>= nf 0)
                           (< (-> *bf-engaged* count) 512)
                           (< (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data nf pos)) BF_ENGAGE_REACH)
                           )
                  (set! (-> *bf-engaged* unit (-> *bf-engaged* count)) (-> info proc))
                  (+! (-> *bf-engaged* count) 1)
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-restore-hatred ()
  "Write back the entries `bf-city-apply-hatred` changed, and take the battle's two hatreds off the
   list when they are still its last."
  (when (and (bf-city-controller?) (-> *bf-city-saved* saved?))
    (let ((saved *bf-city-saved*)
          (table (-> *cty-attack-controller* hatred-indices))
          )
      (dotimes (i 8)
        (dotimes (j 8)
          (set! (-> table (bf-city-hatred-slot (-> *bf-ctt* i) (-> *bf-ctt* j))) (-> saved hatred (+ (* 8 i) j)))
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (when (and (bf-city-controller?)
             (nonzero? (-> *bf-city-saved* vals-length))
             (= (-> *cty-attack-controller* hatred-vals length) (-> *bf-city-saved* vals-length))
             )
    (+! (-> *cty-attack-controller* hatred-vals length) -2)
    )
  (set! (-> *bf-city-saved* vals-length) 0)
  (set! (-> *bf-city-saved* saved?) #f)
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-zone-branch? ((branch nav-branch))
  "#t when nav BRANCH (a lane of a segment, or the one a unit walks) belongs to a city section
   loaded now: it lies in that section's nav-graph branch array (the traffic engine patches each
   segment's branch to point there, traffic-engine.gc level-link). The whole city is the
   battlefield. #f for a missing branch."
  (let ((addr (the-as uint branch))
        (found #f)
        )
    (when (and branch (nonzero? addr))
      (dotimes (i (-> *level* length))
        (let ((lev (-> *level* level i)))
          (when (and (= (-> lev status) 'active) (nonzero? (-> lev bsp)) (nonzero? (-> lev bsp city-level-info)))
            (let ((graph (-> lev bsp city-level-info nav-graph)))
              (if (and (nonzero? graph)
                       (>= addr (the-as uint (-> graph branch-array 0)))
                       (< addr (the-as uint (-> graph branch-array (-> graph branch-count))))
                       )
                  (set! found #t)
                  )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    found
    )
  )

(defun bf-keep-unit? ((unit process))
  "Called by the traffic engine (traffic-engine.gc, its per-frame check of the awake pedestrians)
   for UNIT outside the cells it keeps awake, the ones its camera's visibility marks: the stock
   sends such a unit back to its pool. During a fight, #t keeps it awake wherever the camera is
   while it walks a lane of a loaded section (`bf-city-zone-branch?`): units vanished out of the
   camera's view (the author's notes), and with them the fight the reserves count. One on no lane
   (a flying unit) stays awake."
  (and (bf-fighting?)
       (let ((branch (-> (the-as citizen unit) controller branch)))
         (or (not branch) (zero? (the-as uint branch)) (bf-city-zone-branch? branch))
         )
       )
  )

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Battle points on the streets
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define *bf-city-hatch* (new 'static 'vector))

(defun bf-city-hatch-dir ((pos vector))
  "The way a troop transport over POS opens its hatch: the first of 12 directions, from toward the
   player turning a twelfth either way in turn, whose landing is on the street (bf-transport.gc `bf-transport-landing?`).
   A guard leaves the hatch only onto free nav mesh behind it, pinned to the ship until then.
   Toward the player alone, the ship at the Freedom League's headquarters faced a building and its
   guards never left; along the nearest lane, or toward the zone's middle first, ships stuck at
   bases near the player too, where toward him they had not. Returns `*bf-city-hatch*`, or #f when
   none (the ship then faces the player)."
  (let ((dir *bf-city-hatch*)
        (base (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (target-pos 0) pos))
        (mesh (find-nearest-nav-mesh pos 8192.0))
        (found #f)
        )
    (set! (-> base y) 0.0)
    ;; the player under the ship: the hatch to -z, as the ship faced before (bf-transport.gc)
    (if (< (vector-length base) 409.6)
        (set-vector! base 0.0 0.0 -1.0 1.0)
        )
    (vector-normalize! base 1.0)
    (dotimes (k 12)
      (when (and mesh (not found))
        ;; 0, +30, -30, +60, -60 ... degrees from the player
        (vector-rotate-around-y! dir base (* (degrees 30) (the float (if (logtest? k 1) (/ (+ k 1) 2) (- (/ k 2))))))
        (set! (-> dir w) 1.0)
        (if (bf-transport-landing? pos dir mesh)
            (set! found #t)
            )
        )
      )
    (if found dir)
    )
  )

(define *bf-city-spot* (new 'static 'vector))

(defun bf-city-held-dist ((team int) (pos vector))
  "The distance on the ground from POS to the nearest battle point side TEAM holds (its base
   included), 0.0 for none."
  (let ((best -1.0))
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (when (= (-> *bf* points i owner) team)
        (let ((d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> *bf* points i pos) pos)))
          (if (or (< best 0.0) (< d best))
              (set! best d)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    (fmax 0.0 best)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-front-score ((team int) (i int))
  "How far battle point I stands from the front of side TEAM, lowest first (round 41): its distance
   to TEAM's nearest point plus its distance to the other side's nearest point (0 for one the other
   side holds), plus half their difference. The neutral points halfway between the two sides come
   first, the other side's points nearest TEAM's next; a neutral point gets the same score from
   both sides, so their units head for the same points and meet there. Ranked
   from the bases alone, each side took the points nearest its own and the armies of 100 met
   nowhere in three minutes (round 41's tests)."
  (let* ((pos (-> *bf* points i pos))
         (mine (bf-city-held-dist team pos))
         (theirs (if (= (-> *bf* points i owner) (bf-other-team team))
                     0.0
                     (bf-city-held-dist (bf-other-team team) pos)
                     )
                 )
         )
    (+ mine theirs (* 0.5 (fabs (- mine theirs))))
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-transports ()
  "Twice a second, for each battle point in a loaded section (battlefront.gc `bf-point-live?`):
   - not moved yet: onto the open ground nearest it within 20 m, a base onto the most open within
     30 m (round 45) (bf-transport.gc `bf-transport-spot`: ground, a nav mesh, nothing above up to
     60 m), so the point stands in the open and its ship hovers right over it, through no roof or
     bridge;
   - a base: its side's troop transport stationed over it, its side's place to bring units
     (bf-transport.gc: it drops them while the side lacks some, and stays); a control point gets no
     ship: its holder's units appear on the nav meshes around it (`bf-city-spawn-near`);
   - taken by the other side: its ship leaves (`'leave`), and the new holder's comes once it has
     gone (`old-ship`).
   A point's ship leaves too when its section unloads, and for good once its side's units are all
   brought (battlefront-h.gc `bf-ships-gone?`, round 44) or once it brought `*bf-ship-load*` units
   itself (100: it rises into the sky and none comes to that base again, `ship-done?`, round 45, the
   author's wish). The ships are the director's children."
  (let ((parent (the-as process (handle->process (-> *bf* director)))))
    (when (and parent *target* (bf-fighting?))
      (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
        (let* ((pt (-> *bf* points i))
               (live? (bf-point-live? pt))
               (ship (handle->process (-> pt ship)))
               )
          (when (and live? (not (-> pt snapped?)))
            (set! (-> pt snapped?) #t)
            (when (if (-> pt base?)
                      (bf-transport-spot (-> pt pos) *bf-city-spot* BF_SPOT_REACH #t)
                      (bf-transport-spot (-> pt pos) *bf-city-spot* (meters 20) #f)
                      )
              (format 0 "battlefront: point ~D moved ~M onto open ground~%" i (vector-vector-distance (-> pt pos) *bf-city-spot*))
              (vector-copy! (-> pt pos) *bf-city-spot*)
              )
            )
          ;; its load brought: it leaves for good
          (when (and ship (>= (-> (the-as bf-transport ship) count-units) (the-as uint *bf-ship-load*)))
            (set! (-> pt ship-done?) #t)
            (format 0 "battlefront: the ship over point ~D brought its ~D units~%" i *bf-ship-load*)
            )
          (cond
            ((and ship (or (not live?)
                           (!= (-> (the-as bf-transport ship) team) (-> pt owner))
                           (bf-ships-gone? (-> (the-as bf-transport ship) team))
                           (-> pt ship-done?)
                           )
                  )
             (send-event ship 'leave)
             (set! (-> pt old-ship) (-> pt ship))
             (set! (-> pt ship) (the-as handle #f))
             (format 0 "battlefront: the ship over point ~D leaves~%" i)
             )
            ((and (not ship) live? (-> pt base?) (>= (-> pt owner) 0) (not (handle->process (-> pt old-ship)))
                  (not (bf-ships-gone? (-> pt owner)))
                  (not (-> pt ship-done?))
                  )
             ;; right over the point, which stands on the open spot found (`snapped?`)
             (when (bf-transport-spot (-> pt pos) *bf-city-spot* 0.0 #f)
               (let* ((hatch (bf-city-hatch-dir *bf-city-spot*))
                      (new-ship (bf-transport-spawn parent *bf-city-spot* (-> pt owner) i hatch))
                      )
                 (when new-ship
                   (set! (-> pt ship) (process->handle new-ship))
                   (format 0 "battlefront: side ~D ship over point ~D, ~M from it~%" (-> pt owner) i
                           (vector-vector-xz-distance *bf-city-spot* (-> pt pos)))
                   )
                 )
               )
             )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-ships-down ()
  "Every troop transport of the battle gone at once (the battle's end, a regroup)."
  (dotimes (i BF_POINT_MAX)
    (let ((ship (handle->process (-> *bf* points i ship)))
          (old (handle->process (-> *bf* points i old-ship)))
          )
      (if ship
          (deactivate ship)
          )
      (if old
          (deactivate old)
          )
      (set! (-> *bf* points i ship) (the-as handle #f))
      (set! (-> *bf* points i old-ship) (the-as handle #f))
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; a unit heads for one of this many points its side does not hold, drawn at random: every one since
;; round 42 (the author's wish: the units spread over the objectives, the conflict over the whole
;; city), the 3 nearest the front in round 41, the 3 nearest its base before
(defconstant BF_GOAL_PICK BF_POINT_MAX)

(defun bf-city-owners-key ()
  "A number that changes whenever a point changes hands: each point's owner, two bits a point,
   kept under 65521 (a prime). Unbounded, the 17 points of Jak 2's city made it pass 2^32, and the
   goal draw's `mod` (32-bit) went negative: nearly every unit drew no point and went to its side's
   nearest held one (round 42's tests: each side's guards on one or two points)."
  (let ((key 0))
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (set! key (mod (+ (* key 4) (+ (-> *bf* points i owner) 1)) 65521))
      )
    key
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-goal-point ((team int) (pick int))
  "A control point side TEAM does not hold, its units' objective (battlefront.gc `bf-update-points`
   captures it once they hold it): of the BF_GOAL_PICK such points nearest TEAM's front (every one
   since round 42; `bf-city-front-score`, round 41; nearest its base before), number
   PICK modulo how many, from the nearest. Ranked from the sides' points, not from the unit, a pick
   holds while the unit walks: ranked from the unit, the second nearest became the nearest on the
   way, and the unit turned to another. -1 when TEAM holds every one."
  (let ((n 0)
        (taken 0)
        (best -1)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (if (and (not (-> *bf* points i base?)) (!= (-> *bf* points i owner) team))
          (+! n 1)
          )
      )
    (when (> n 0)
      (dotimes (r (+ (mod pick (min n BF_GOAL_PICK)) 1))
        (set! best -1)
        (let ((best-d 0.0))
          (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
            (let ((pt (-> *bf* points i)))
              (when (and (not (-> pt base?)) (!= (-> pt owner) team) (not (logtest? taken (ash 1 i))))
                (let ((d (bf-city-front-score team i)))
                  (when (or (< best 0) (< d best-d))
                    (set! best i)
                    (set! best-d d)
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        (set! taken (logior taken (ash 1 best)))
        )
      )
    best
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-guard-point ((team int) (from vector))
  "The control point nearest FROM that side TEAM holds in a loaded section (battlefront.gc
   `bf-point-live?`): the one its defenders keep. -1 for none."
  (let ((best -1)
        (best-d 0.0)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (let ((pt (-> *bf* points i)))
        (when (and (not (-> pt base?)) (= (-> pt owner) team) (bf-point-live? pt))
          (let ((d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> pt pos) from)))
            (when (or (< best 0) (< d best-d))
              (set! best i)
              (set! best-d d)
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    best
    )
  )

(defconstant BF_CONTEST_RATIO 3) ;; a side's units come to a contested point while fewer than this many per foe, plus 2, stand in its zone

(defun bf-city-contested-point ((team int) (from vector))
  "The contested control point nearest FROM within BF_CONTEST_REACH for side TEAM: units of the other
   side stand in its zone (BF_ZONE_REACH, `*bf-zone-near*`) while TEAM's units stand there too or
   TEAM holds it: its defenders come as the attackers do, before the capture starts. With the
   capture radius (15 m) alone, no point was ever fought over in 10 minutes: the attackers took
   them empty. From outside its zone, only while TEAM has fewer than BF_CONTEST_RATIO units per foe,
   plus 2, in it: every unit within 250 m came, and 25 of a side stood at one point held against a
   foe or two out of their sight (round 27's tests). -1 for none."
  (let ((best -1)
        (best-d 0.0)
        (foe (bf-other-team team))
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (let ((pt (-> *bf* points i)))
        (when (and (not (-> pt base?))
                   (> (-> *bf-zone-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX foe) i)) 0)
                   (or (> (-> *bf-zone-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX team) i)) 0) (= (-> pt owner) team))
                   )
          (let ((d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> pt pos) from)))
            (when (and (< d BF_CONTEST_REACH)
                       (or (< best 0) (< d best-d))
                       (or (< d BF_ZONE_REACH)
                           (< (-> *bf-zone-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX team) i))
                              (+ 2 (* BF_CONTEST_RATIO (-> *bf-zone-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX foe) i))))
                              )
                           )
                       )
              (set! best i)
              (set! best-d d)
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    best
    )
  )

;; Each unit keeps its goal (`bf-city-sticky-goal`) until its side holds it, or it is stuck.
(defconstant BF_GOAL_SLOTS 512)            ;; units the goals keep, by process id (256 until round 44)
(defconstant BF_STUCK_TIME (seconds 10))   ;; a unit that has not moved BF_STUCK_MOVE in this long, away from its point and out of a fight, takes another goal
(defconstant BF_STUCK_MOVE (meters 3))
(defconstant BF_STUCK_HOP (seconds 4))        ;; a marching unit stuck this long near its waypoint is put onto it (`bf-march-apply`; 8 s until round 31: guards still piled up between the Industrial Zone and the Slums, the author's play)
(defconstant BF_STUCK_HOP_REACH (meters 20))  ;; 15 m until round 31
(define *bf-stuck-hops* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0)) ;; for the tests: units put onto their waypoint
(define *bf-crossings* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0))  ;; for the tests: units onto their next mesh by its ground (`bf-march-cross!`)

(deftype bf-goals (structure)
  "The units' goals (`bf-city-sticky-goal`), by process id (BF_GOAL_SLOTS)."
  ((unit  handle     BF_GOAL_SLOTS)
   (goal  int8       BF_GOAL_SLOTS)
   (salt  int32      BF_GOAL_SLOTS)   ;; how many times it drew again for being stuck
   (time  time-frame BF_GOAL_SLOTS)   ;; when it last moved BF_STUCK_MOVE (or drew)
   (pos   vector     BF_GOAL_SLOTS :inline)
   )
  )

(define *bf-goals* (new 'static 'bf-goals))

;; no unit yet: a 0 handle is read as a process at address 0 and crashes (Lisp wiki common.md)
(dotimes (i BF_GOAL_SLOTS)
  (set! (-> *bf-goals* unit i) (the-as handle #f))
  )

(defun bf-city-sticky-goal ((proc process) (team int))
  "The control point unit PROC of side TEAM conquers (`bf-city-unit-goal`): drawn once
   (`bf-city-goal-point`) and kept until its side holds it. Drawn again at each change of hands
   (round 27), the units turned back at every capture, one spider going for points 7, 3, 8, 4 in
   turn (round 29's tests). A unit that has not moved BF_STUCK_MOVE in BF_STUCK_TIME, more than
   20 m from its point and out of a fight, draws another (its salt): units stood 35 to 80 s at
   the same spot on their way, at the Port Gate's and the Industrial Zone's seams (round 29's
   tests). -1 when its side holds every control point."
  (let* ((g *bf-goals*)
         (k (logand (-> proc pid) (+ BF_GOAL_SLOTS -1)))
         (h (process->handle proc))
         (now (-> *display* game-clock frame-counter))
         (here (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root trans))
         )
    (when (!= (-> g unit k) h)
      (set! (-> g unit k) h)
      (set! (-> g goal k) -1)
      (set! (-> g salt k) 0)
      (vector-copy! (-> g pos k) here)
      (set! (-> g time k) now)
      )
    (let ((cur (-> g goal k)))
      ;; moving, near its point or fighting: not stuck
      (when (or (< BF_STUCK_MOVE (vector-vector-xz-distance here (-> g pos k)))
                (bf-city-engaged? proc)
                (and (>= cur 0) (< (vector-vector-xz-distance here (-> *bf* points cur pos)) (meters 20)))
                )
        (vector-copy! (-> g pos k) here)
        (set! (-> g time k) now)
        )
      (when (< BF_STUCK_TIME (- now (-> g time k)))
        (+! (-> g salt k) 1)
        (set! cur -1)
        (vector-copy! (-> g pos k) here)
        (set! (-> g time k) now)
        )
      (when (or (< cur 0) (>= cur (-> *bf* point-count)) (-> *bf* points cur base?) (= (-> *bf* points cur owner) team))
        (set! cur (bf-city-goal-point team (+ (-> proc pid) (* 7 (-> g salt k)) (bf-city-owners-key))))
        (set! (-> g goal k) cur)
        )
      cur
      )
    )
  )

(defconstant BF_HUNT_WEST (meters 1968)) ;; Spargus: a foe west of this stands on the west district's meshes (the pass's gap, 1958 to 1977 m)

(defun bf-city-hunt ((proc process) (out vector))
  "Spargus's destruction of an objective (round 55, the author's wish: the Freedom League's units do
   not wait around the artifact, they hunt every Krimzon Guard unit): OUT, the place of the unit of
   the Krimzon Guard (or its player) nearest PROC (`*bf-unit-dots*`), else the Krimzon Guard's camp.
   Returns the point the march routes by, the one of the district OUT stands in: the artifact's
   (west of BF_HUNT_WEST) or the Krimzon Guard's camp (east). No side effect but OUT."
  (let ((dots *bf-unit-dots*)
        (from (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root trans))
        (best -1)
        (best-d 0.0)
        )
    (dotimes (d (-> dots count))
      (when (= (-> dots team d) BF_TEAM_KG)
        (let ((dist (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> dots pos d) from)))
          (when (or (< best 0) (< dist best-d))
            (set! best d)
            (set! best-d dist)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (vector-copy! out (if (>= best 0) (-> dots pos best) (-> *bf* points 1 pos)))
    (if (< (-> out x) BF_HUNT_WEST) BF_ARTIFACT_POINT 1)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-unit-goal ((proc process) (team int))
  "The point unit PROC of side TEAM heads for, as Star Wars Battlefront's units take the command
   posts: a contested point near it first (`bf-city-contested-point`), to clear it of the other
   side's units so the capture can go on; else the control point it guards, while its side holds it
   and the other side's units come within BF_THREAT_REACH of it (bf-transport.gc `bf-post-point`:
   one unit in four brought there; with no foe coming, the guards stood around the point already
   taken, the author's play, round 26); else one of the points its side does not hold
   (`bf-city-goal-point`, BF_GOAL_PICK: all of them since round 42), to conquer it, drawn at random
   by its process id and the points' owners (`bf-city-owners-key`): the units spread over the
   objectives (the author's wish, rounds 27 and 42: before, all went for the nearest but 3 in 10); kept until its side holds it, or drawn
   again when the unit is stuck (`bf-city-sticky-goal`, round 29); with every control point held,
   the one nearest it (`bf-city-guard-point`). In Spargus's destruction of an objective the Freedom
   League's units hunt instead (`bf-city-hunt`, round 55). -1 for none."
  (if (and (= team BF_TEAM_FF) (bf-objective?))
      (return (bf-city-hunt proc (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      )
  (let* ((pos (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root trans))
         (contest (bf-city-contested-point team pos))
         (post (bf-post-point proc))
         )
    (cond
      ((>= contest 0) contest)
      ((and (>= post 0)
            (= (-> *bf* points post owner) team)
            (> (-> *bf-threat-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX (bf-other-team team)) post)) 0)
            )
       post
       )
      (else
        (let ((goal (bf-city-sticky-goal proc team)))
          (if (>= goal 0)
              goal
              (bf-city-guard-point team pos)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defconstant BF_ROUTE_NODES 256) ;; lane nodes a route search looks at, at most

(deftype bf-route-work (structure)
  "The lane nodes a route search reached (`bf-city-route`), each with the first lane of its way."
  ((node   nav-node   BF_ROUTE_NODES)
   (first  nav-branch BF_ROUTE_NODES)
   )
  )

(define *bf-route-work* (new 'static 'bf-route-work))

(defun bf-city-route ((from nav-node) (goal vector))
  "The lane out of lane node FROM on the way to GOAL: a search breadth first over the lanes a
   faction may walk (dest-node-id-at-max?), BF_ROUTE_NODES nodes at most, through every loaded
   section (a section's links lead into the next one's graph), keeping the node reached nearest
   GOAL; the first lane of the way to it. A choice at each junction of the lane ending nearest the
   goal left the units in dead ends and detours, 140 to 200 m from a point next door. #f when no
   lane leaves FROM."
  (let ((w *bf-route-work*)
        (n 0)
        (head 0)
        (best -1)
        (best-d 0.0)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> from branch-count))
      (let ((b (-> from branch-array i)))
        (when (and (< n BF_ROUTE_NODES) (dest-node-id-at-max? b))
          (set! (-> w node n) (-> b dest-node))
          (set! (-> w first n) b)
          (+! n 1)
          )
        )
      )
    (while (< head n)
      (let* ((node (-> w node head))
             (d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> node position) goal))
             )
        (when (or (< best 0) (< d best-d))
          (set! best head)
          (set! best-d d)
          )
        (dotimes (i (-> node branch-count))
          (let ((b (-> node branch-array i)))
            (when (and (< n BF_ROUTE_NODES) (dest-node-id-at-max? b))
              (let* ((next (-> b dest-node))
                     (seen? (= next from))
                     )
                (dotimes (k n)
                  (if (= (-> w node k) next)
                      (set! seen? #t)
                      )
                  )
                (when (not seen?)
                  (set! (-> w node n) next)
                  (set! (-> w first n) (-> w first head))
                  (+! n 1)
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      (+! head 1)
      )
    (if (>= best 0)
        (-> w first best)
        )
    )
  )

;; The units' march to their point over the nav meshes (`bf-city-steer`, `bf-march-apply`). The
;; city's walking lanes are loops within a section: the Freedom League's base, in ctyslumc, has 138
;; lane nodes and no lane out of the section, and 173 of ctyslumb's 177 nodes have one lane out or
;; none; a citizen at a lane's dead end jumps to any lane 20 to 120 m behind it (citizen-method-208).
;; The lanes alone kept the units 140 to 290 m from a point next door. The meshes join the sections:
;; a nav-enemy standing on a mesh's link poly moves onto the next mesh (nav-enemy-method-188).
(defconstant BF_MARCH_MAX 512)          ;; units marching at once, at most (200 a side since round 44)
(defconstant BF_MARCH_NEAR (meters 12)) ;; a unit this close to its point walks the lanes around it
(defconstant BF_WAY_MESHES 768)         ;; nav meshes of the active levels the ways know, at most

(deftype bf-march (structure)
  "The units marching to their point, each with where it runs now (just past the link poly into its
   next mesh, or the point) and the mesh it was on then."
  ((count  int32)
   (unit   handle   BF_MARCH_MAX)
   (from   nav-mesh BF_MARCH_MAX)
   (to     vector   BF_MARCH_MAX :inline)
   (hop    int16    BF_MARCH_MAX)     ;; the bridge it crosses at `to` (100 + 2 k + side), -1 none
   (point  int16    BF_MARCH_MAX)     ;; the battle point it marches to
   (goal   nav-mesh BF_POINT_MAX)     ;; each point's mesh this tick, #f for none loaded
   )
  )

(defconstant BF_BRIDGE_MAX 8)           ;; bridges between meshes the ways know, at most
(defconstant BF_BRIDGE_GAP (meters 6))  ;; two meshes this close, with no link, get a bridge
;; A unit this close to a bridge's end crosses it. At 2.5 m (until round 27) the guards stopped 3.5 to
;; 4.5 m from the end between Slums B and Slums A, an end 1.5 m inside its poly from a corner, and
;; waited there up to 24 s, two at a time (the author's play, round 28's tests)
(defconstant BF_BRIDGE_HOP (meters 6))

(deftype bf-ways (structure)
  "The way to each battle point from every nav mesh of the active levels (`bf-ways-build`): for
   point i and mesh k of `mesh`, `next` (at BF_WAY_MESHES i + k) holds the link of mesh k a unit
   takes toward the point, 100 + 2 b + s to cross bridge b from its side s (0 its mesh-a, 1 its
   mesh-b), -2 on the point's own mesh, -1 for no way. A bridge joins two meshes that touch with no
   link between them (`bf-ways-bridges`): a unit at one end (`end-a`, `end-b`, each 1.5 m inside
   its mesh) moves to the other (`bf-march-apply`)."
  ((count         int32)
   (time          time-frame)                     ;; last build
   (mesh          nav-mesh BF_WAY_MESHES)
   (next          int16    13056)                 ;; BF_POINT_MAX (17) times BF_WAY_MESHES
   (depth         int16    13056)                 ;; the same: meshes from it to the point's (0 its own)
   (queue         int16    BF_WAY_MESHES)
   (prev          nav-mesh BF_WAY_MESHES)         ;; the meshes listed when the bridges were made
   (prev-count    int32)
   (deck-y        float    BF_WAY_MESHES)         ;; each mesh's upper deck: its polys over this height (`bf-deck-via`), far up for none
   (bridge-count  int32)
   (mesh-a        int16    BF_BRIDGE_MAX)
   (mesh-b        int16    BF_BRIDGE_MAX)
   (end-a         vector   BF_BRIDGE_MAX :inline)
   (end-b         vector   BF_BRIDGE_MAX :inline)
   )
  )

(define *bf-ways* (new 'static 'bf-ways))

;; The upper decks: a mesh's polys BF_DECK_RISE over its most common height, 4 at least (the
;; Industrial Zone's walkways, 27 m up its stairs from the 8 m streets). One guard in BF_DECK_SHARE
;; goes by them once on its way through that mesh (`bf-deck-via`), when that way is at most
;; BF_DECK_DETOUR times the direct one plus 20 m: by the streets alone, the shortest ways, no unit
;; ever went up there (the author's play, round 26).
(defconstant BF_DECK_RISE (meters 8))
(defconstant BF_DECK_SHARE 3)
(defconstant BF_DECK_DETOUR 1.6)
(defconstant BF_DECK_DONE_MAX 512) ;; 200 units a side at most since round 44

(deftype bf-deck-done (structure)
  "The guards that have been on a mesh's upper deck on their way: each one's handle and that mesh."
  ((unit  handle   BF_DECK_DONE_MAX)
   (mesh  nav-mesh BF_DECK_DONE_MAX)
   (next  int32)
   )
  )

(define *bf-deck-done* (new 'static 'bf-deck-done))

(dotimes (i BF_DECK_DONE_MAX)
  (set! (-> *bf-deck-done* unit i) (the-as handle #f))
  )

(defun bf-deck-done? ((unit process) (m nav-mesh))
  "#t when UNIT has been on mesh M's upper deck (`*bf-deck-done*`)."
  (let ((h (process->handle unit))
        (d *bf-deck-done*)
        )
    (dotimes (i BF_DECK_DONE_MAX)
      (if (and (= (-> d unit i) h) (= (-> d mesh i) m))
          (return #t)
          )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-deck-done! ((unit process) (m nav-mesh))
  "UNIT has been on mesh M's upper deck: it goes on (`bf-deck-via`)."
  (let* ((d *bf-deck-done*)
         (n (-> d next))
         )
    (set! (-> d unit n) (process->handle unit))
    (set! (-> d mesh n) m)
    (set! (-> d next) (mod (+ n 1) BF_DECK_DONE_MAX))
    )
  (none)
  )

(define *bf-march* (new 'static 'bf-march))

;; For the tests (docs/modding/current_mod/battlefront_smoke.gc, `bf-city-roll-sample`): robotguards
;; marching far from their point, those of them on their ball clip, those faster than 24 m/s;
;; robotguards in the stock roll-chase, those of them rolling at BF_ROLL_SCALE times its 20 m/s.
(define *bf-roll-sample* (new 'static 'array int32 5 0 0 0 0 0))

(defun bf-city-roll-sample ()
  "Adds the battle's robotguards now to `*bf-roll-sample*`: [0] marching more than BF_ROLL_REACH
   plus 5 m from their point, [1] of them with the ball as run clip, [2] of them faster than
   24 m/s, [3] in 'roll-chase, [4] of them aimed at over 28 m/s."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*))
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (= (-> proc type symbol) 'roboguard-city) (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0))
                (let ((unit (the-as citizen proc))
                      (w *bf-march*)
                      )
                  (when (-> unit nav)
                    (dotimes (j (-> w count))
                      (when (and (= (-> w unit j) (process->handle proc)) (>= (-> w point j) 0)
                                 (< (+ BF_ROLL_REACH (meters 5))
                                    (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> *bf* points (-> w point j) pos))
                                    )
                                 )
                        (+! (-> *bf-roll-sample* 0) 1)
                        (if (= (-> unit anim-run) BF_ROBOT_BALL_CLIP)
                            (+! (-> *bf-roll-sample* 1) 1)
                            )
                        (if (< (meters 24) (-> unit nav state speed))
                            (+! (-> *bf-roll-sample* 2) 1)
                            )
                        )
                      )
                    (when (and (-> unit next-state) (= (-> unit next-state name) 'roll-chase))
                      (+! (-> *bf-roll-sample* 3) 1)
                      (if (< (meters 28) (-> unit nav target-speed))
                          (+! (-> *bf-roll-sample* 4) 1)
                          )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  0
  )

(defun bf-march-link-poly ((m nav-mesh) (link int) (out vector))
  "OUT gets the centroid of mesh M's poly for LINK (pat 4, its link field LINK): a nav-enemy standing
   on it moves onto the mesh beyond (nav-enemy-method-188). #f when M has none."
  (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
    (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
      (when (and (logtest? (-> poly pat) 4) (= (-> poly link) link))
        (poly-centroid m poly out)
        (return #t)
        )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-march-through ((m nav-mesh) (link int) (out vector))
  "OUT gets a spot 2 m past mesh M's poly for LINK toward the next mesh's own link poly: a unit sent
   there walks onto the link poly and across, where its own centroid would stop it short of it (the
   units crowded there). #f when M has no poly for LINK."
  (when (bf-march-link-poly m link out)
    (let* ((lk (-> m link-array link))
           (dest (-> lk dest-mesh))
           (there (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
           )
      (when (and dest (< (-> lk dest-link-poly-id) (-> dest poly-count)))
        (poly-centroid dest (-> dest poly-array (-> lk dest-link-poly-id)) there)
        (let ((dir (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) there out)))
          (set! (-> dir y) 0.0)
          (when (< (meters 0.1) (vector-length dir))
            (vector-normalize! dir (meters 2))
            (vector+! out out dir)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    #t
    )
  )

(defun bf-ways-index ((m nav-mesh))
  "Index of nav mesh M in `*bf-ways*` mesh, -1 when it is not listed."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*))
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (if (= (-> w mesh k) m)
          (return k)
          )
      )
    )
  -1
  )

(defun bf-ways-linked? ((a nav-mesh) (b nav-mesh))
  "#t when one of mesh A's links leads to mesh B."
  (dotimes (l (-> a link-count))
    (if (= (-> a link-array l dest-mesh) b)
        (return #t)
        )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-ways-bridges ()
  "The bridges of `*bf-ways*`: each pair of listed meshes with no link either way whose polys come
   within BF_BRIDGE_GAP of each other (a corner of one poly from a corner of the other, among the
   pair of polys whose centers are nearest), its ends 1.5 m inside each poly from those corners.
   The streets of Freedom HQ (ctyslumb) and the Slums (ctysluma) meet there with no link: the
   south's two meshes linked to the rest of the city only through the unloaded ruins, and its
   units could never reach a point of the north, nor the north's units one of the south."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (pa (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (pb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (ca (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (cb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (va (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (vb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (set! (-> w bridge-count) 0)
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (dotimes (j (-> w count))
        (let ((ma (-> w mesh i))
              (mb (-> w mesh j))
              )
          (when (and (< i j)
                     (< (-> w bridge-count) BF_BRIDGE_MAX)
                     (not (bf-ways-linked? ma mb))
                     (not (bf-ways-linked? mb ma))
                     ;; their bounding spheres overlap or nearly
                     (< (vector-vector-distance (the-as vector (-> ma bounds)) (the-as vector (-> mb bounds)))
                        (+ (-> ma bounds r) (-> mb bounds r) BF_BRIDGE_GAP)
                        )
                     )
            (let ((best -1.0)
                  (best-a -1)
                  (best-b -1)
                  )
              ;; the polys whose centers are nearest
              (dotimes (x (-> ma poly-count))
                (poly-centroid ma (-> ma poly-array x) pa)
                (dotimes (y (-> mb poly-count))
                  (poly-centroid mb (-> mb poly-array y) pb)
                  (let ((d (vector-vector-distance pa pb)))
                    (when (or (< best 0.0) (< d best))
                      (set! best d)
                      (set! best-a x)
                      (set! best-b y)
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              (when (>= best-a 0)
                (let ((polya (-> ma poly-array best-a))
                      (polyb (-> mb poly-array best-b))
                      (gap -1.0)
                      )
                  (poly-centroid ma polya ca)
                  (poly-centroid mb polyb cb)
                  ;; their nearest corners
                  (dotimes (x (the-as int (-> polya vertex-count)))
                    (dotimes (y (the-as int (-> polyb vertex-count)))
                      (vector+! pa (-> polya vertex x) (the-as vector (-> ma bounds)))
                      (vector+! pb (-> polyb vertex y) (the-as vector (-> mb bounds)))
                      (let ((d (vector-vector-distance pa pb)))
                        (when (or (< gap 0.0) (< d gap))
                          (set! gap d)
                          (vector-copy! va pa)
                          (vector-copy! vb pb)
                          )
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  (when (and (>= gap 0.0) (< gap BF_BRIDGE_GAP))
                    (let ((k (-> w bridge-count)))
                      (set! (-> w mesh-a k) i)
                      (set! (-> w mesh-b k) j)
                      ;; 1.5 m inside each poly from its corner, toward its center
                      (vector+! (-> w end-a k) va (vector-normalize! (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) ca va) (meters 1.5)))
                      (vector+! (-> w end-b k) vb (vector-normalize! (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) cb vb) (meters 1.5)))
                      (format 0 "battlefront: bridge ~D between meshes ~D and ~D, corners ~M apart~%" k i j gap)
                      (+! (-> w bridge-count) 1)
                      )
                    )
                  (when (and (>= gap BF_BRIDGE_GAP) (< best (meters 40)))
                    (format 0 "battlefront: no bridge between meshes ~D and ~D, corners ~M apart" i j gap)
                    (format 0 " at ~M ~M ~M and ~M ~M ~M~%" (-> va x) (-> va y) (-> va z) (-> vb x) (-> vb y) (-> vb z))
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-build ()
  "Every 10 s of a fight: list the nav meshes of the active levels (their bsp nav-meshes), then for
   each battle point a search breadth first from its own mesh (`*bf-march*` goal) over the meshes'
   links, unbounded: each mesh reached keeps its own link back toward the mesh it was reached from
   (the links join two meshes both ways). A unit then finds the first link of its way to any point
   in its own mesh's entry (`bf-march-waypoint`). A search from each unit's mesh, 96 then 160
   meshes at most, found no way from the Freedom League's base once the whole city was loaded: its
   guards stayed between their base and Freedom HQ, no one of them marching."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (march *bf-march*)
        )
    (set! (-> w count) 0)
    (dotimes (li (-> *level* length))
      (let ((lev (-> *level* level li)))
        (when (= (-> lev status) 'active)
          (let ((meshes (-> lev bsp nav-meshes)))
            (when (nonzero? meshes)
              (dotimes (i (-> meshes length))
                (let ((m (-> meshes i nav-mesh)))
                  (when (and m (< (-> w count) BF_WAY_MESHES))
                    (set! (-> w mesh (-> w count)) m)
                    (+! (-> w count) 1)
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    ;; each mesh's upper deck (`bf-deck-via`): its polys BF_DECK_RISE over its most common height
    ;; (5 m bands), 4 at least
    (let ((band (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 24))
          (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          )
      (dotimes (k (-> w count))
        (let ((m (-> w mesh k))
              (best 0)
              (bk 0)
              (above 0)
              )
          (dotimes (b 24)
            (set! (-> band b) 0)
            )
          (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
            (poly-centroid m (-> m poly-array i) c)
            (+! (-> band (max 0 (min 23 (the int (/ (+ (-> c y) (meters 40)) (meters 5)))))) 1)
            )
          (dotimes (b 24)
            (when (< best (-> band b))
              (set! best (-> band b))
              (set! bk b)
              )
            )
          (let ((deck (+ (- (* (+ (the float bk) 0.5) (meters 5)) (meters 40)) BF_DECK_RISE)))
            (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
              (poly-centroid m (-> m poly-array i) c)
              (if (< deck (-> c y))
                  (+! above 1)
                  )
              )
            (set! (-> w deck-y k) (if (>= above 4) deck (meters 100000)))
            )
          )
        )
      )
    ;; the bridges again when the meshes listed changed (a search over every pair of polys)
    (let ((same? (= (-> w count) (-> w prev-count))))
      (dotimes (k (-> w count))
        (if (!= (-> w mesh k) (-> w prev k))
            (set! same? #f)
            )
        )
      (when (not same?)
        (dotimes (k (-> w count))
          (set! (-> w prev k) (-> w mesh k))
          )
        (set! (-> w prev-count) (-> w count))
        (bf-ways-bridges)
        )
      )
    (dotimes (pt (-> *bf* point-count))
      (let ((base (* pt BF_WAY_MESHES))
            (g (bf-ways-index (-> march goal pt)))
            (head 0)
            (tail 0)
            )
        (dotimes (k (-> w count))
          (set! (-> w next (+ base k)) -1)
          (set! (-> w depth (+ base k)) -1)
          )
        (when (>= g 0)
          (set! (-> w next (+ base g)) -2)
          (set! (-> w depth (+ base g)) 0)
          (set! (-> w queue 0) g)
          (set! tail 1)
          (while (< head tail)
            (let ((cur (-> w mesh (-> w queue head))))
              (dotimes (l (-> cur link-count))
                (let* ((nb (-> cur link-array l dest-mesh))
                       (nbi (if nb (bf-ways-index nb) -1))
                       )
                  (when (and (>= nbi 0) (= (-> w next (+ base nbi)) -1))
                    ;; the neighbour's own link back to this mesh
                    (dotimes (b (-> nb link-count))
                      (when (= (-> nb link-array b dest-mesh) cur)
                        (set! (-> w next (+ base nbi)) b)
                        (set! (-> w depth (+ base nbi)) (+ (-> w depth (+ base (-> w queue head))) 1))
                        (set! (-> w queue tail) nbi)
                        (+! tail 1)
                        (set! b (the-as int (-> nb link-count)))
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              ;; and over the bridges: the mesh at the other end crosses back to this one
              (let ((ci (-> w queue head)))
                (dotimes (k (-> w bridge-count))
                  (let ((other (cond
                                 ((= (-> w mesh-a k) ci) (-> w mesh-b k))
                                 ((= (-> w mesh-b k) ci) (-> w mesh-a k))
                                 (else -1)
                                 )
                               )
                        )
                    (when (and (>= other 0) (= (-> w next (+ base other)) -1))
                      ;; from the other end's side: 0 when it is the bridge's mesh-a
                      (set! (-> w next (+ base other)) (+ 100 (* 2 k) (if (= (-> w mesh-a k) other) 0 1)))
                      (set! (-> w depth (+ base other)) (+ (-> w depth (+ base ci)) 1))
                      (set! (-> w queue tail) other)
                      (+! tail 1)
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            (+! head 1)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (set-time! (-> w time))
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-march-link ((m nav-mesh) (k int) (goal int) (pid int) (first int))
  "The link of mesh M (`*bf-ways*` mesh K) unit PID crosses toward point GOAL: one of the links of M
   that lead a mesh nearer the point (`depth`), the same one for a unit each time (by its process
   id), so the units take the several streets and meshes a way can go by; FIRST (the search's own)
   when it has no other."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (base (* goal BF_WAY_MESHES))
        (n 0)
        )
    (let ((want (+ (-> w depth (+ base k)) -1)))
      (dotimes (l (-> m link-count))
        (let* ((nb (-> m link-array l dest-mesh))
               (nbi (if nb (bf-ways-index nb) -1))
               )
          (if (and (>= nbi 0) (= (-> w depth (+ base nbi)) want))
              (+! n 1)
              )
          )
        )
      (when (> n 1)
        (let ((pick (mod (+ pid goal) n)))
          (dotimes (l (-> m link-count))
            (let* ((nb (-> m link-array l dest-mesh))
                   (nbi (if nb (bf-ways-index nb) -1))
                   )
              (when (and (>= nbi 0) (= (-> w depth (+ base nbi)) want))
                (if (zero? pick)
                    (return l)
                    )
                (+! pick -1)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    first
    )
  )

(defun bf-deck-via ((unit nav-enemy) (k int) (out vector))
  "In `bf-march-waypoint`: one guard in BF_DECK_SHARE (by its process id) on mesh K of the ways,
   when it has an upper deck (`*bf-ways*` deck-y), goes by it once on its way: OUT, where it runs,
   becomes the middle of the deck's poly that makes its shortest way to OUT, when that way is at
   most BF_DECK_DETOUR times the direct one plus 20 m and OUT is 40 m away or more. On the deck, or
   at that poly, the unit has been there (`bf-deck-done!`) and goes on to OUT as before."
  (let ((m (-> unit nav state mesh)))
    (when (and m
               (>= k 0)
               (= (-> unit type symbol) 'crimson-guard)
               (= (mod (-> unit pid) BF_DECK_SHARE) 1)
               (< (-> *bf-ways* deck-y k) (meters 1000))
               (not (bf-deck-done? unit m))
               )
      (let ((deck (-> *bf-ways* deck-y k))
            (poly (-> unit nav state current-poly))
            (pos (-> unit root trans))
            (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            )
        (if poly
            (poly-centroid m poly c)
            (vector-copy! c pos)
            )
        (cond
          ((< deck (-> c y))
           ;; on the deck: done, on its way again
           (bf-deck-done! unit m)
           )
          (else
            (let ((direct (vector-vector-xz-distance pos out))
                  (best 0.0)
                  (bi -1)
                  )
              (when (< (meters 40) direct)
                (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
                  (poly-centroid m (-> m poly-array i) c)
                  (when (< deck (-> c y))
                    (let ((d (+ (vector-vector-xz-distance pos c) (vector-vector-xz-distance c out))))
                      (when (or (< bi 0) (< d best))
                        (set! best d)
                        (set! bi i)
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                (when (and (>= bi 0) (< best (+ (* BF_DECK_DETOUR direct) (meters 20))))
                  (poly-centroid m (-> m poly-array bi) c)
                  (if (and (< (vector-vector-xz-distance pos c) (meters 5)) (< (fabs (- (-> pos y) (-> c y))) (meters 3)))
                      (bf-deck-done! unit m)
                      (vector-copy! out c)
                      )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define-extern bf-march-target (function nav-enemy int vector vector nav-mesh int int symbol))

(defun bf-march-waypoint ((unit nav-enemy) (goal int) (pos vector) (out vector))
  "Where UNIT runs now on its way to point GOAL at POS: POS itself on the point's mesh; else just
   past the link poly of its own mesh that starts its way there (`*bf-ways*`, `bf-march-through`),
   or the end of a bridge on its mesh (`bf-ways-bridges`); for one guard in three, by the upper deck
   of its mesh first (`bf-deck-via`). #f when no way."
  (let* ((m (-> unit nav state mesh))
         (k (if m (bf-ways-index m) -1))
         (nx (if (>= k 0) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* goal BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -1))
         (ok (bf-march-target unit goal pos out m k nx))
         )
    (if ok
        (bf-deck-via unit k out)
        )
    ok
    )
  )

(defun bf-march-target ((unit nav-enemy) (goal int) (pos vector) (out vector) (m nav-mesh) (k int) (nx int))
  "`bf-march-waypoint` before the deck: OUT, the point or the way's next link or bridge."
  (begin
    (cond
      ((= nx -2)
       (vector-copy! out pos)
       #t
       )
      ((>= nx 100)
       (let ((b (/ (- nx 100) 2)))
         (vector-copy! out (if (zero? (logand (- nx 100) 1)) (-> *bf-ways* end-a b) (-> *bf-ways* end-b b)))
         )
       #t
       )
      ((>= nx 0)
       (bf-march-through m (bf-march-link m k goal (-> unit pid) nx) out)
       )
      (else
        #f
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-marching? ((unit process))
  "#t when UNIT marches now (`*bf-march*`)."
  (let ((h (process->handle unit))
        (w *bf-march*)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (if (= (-> w unit i) h)
          (return #t)
          )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-city-walking? ((unit process))
  "#t when UNIT walks its lanes: the citizens' 'active, or a spider robot's 'hunting, its 'active
   while the faction manager has it at war (spydroid.gc, its 'active goes there with a nonzero
   faction-mode): it follows its dest-point the same way. Taking 'active alone, no spider ever
   marched to its point."
  (and (-> unit next-state)
       (or (= (-> unit next-state name) 'active) (= (-> unit next-state name) 'hunting))
       )
  )

(defun bf-city-zone-foe ((team int) (i int) (from vector) (out vector))
  "OUT: the place of the unit of the other side than TEAM in point I's zone (BF_ZONE_REACH,
   `*bf-unit-dots*`) nearest FROM. Returns #f when none stands there."
  (let ((dots *bf-unit-dots*)
        (best -1)
        (best-d 0.0)
        )
    (dotimes (d (-> dots count))
      (when (and (!= (-> dots team d) team)
                 (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> dots pos d) (-> *bf* points i pos)) BF_ZONE_REACH)
                 )
        (let ((dist (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> dots pos d) from)))
          (when (or (< best 0) (< dist best-d))
            (set! best d)
            (set! best-d dist)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (when (>= best 0)
      (vector-copy! out (-> dots pos best))
      #t
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-march-plan ((unit citizen) (team int))
  "In `bf-city-steer`: UNIT of side TEAM, with no foe in sight (`bf-city-engaged?`: it fights that
   one first), walking its lanes (`bf-city-walking?`) more than BF_MARCH_NEAR from
   its point (`bf-city-unit-goal`) in a loaded section, marches there: `*bf-march*` gets it with its
   waypoint (`bf-march-waypoint`) and its mesh now. With units of the other side in the point's
   zone, it marches at the nearest of them (`bf-city-zone-foe`) instead of the point's middle: sent
   to the middle, the defenders of a point stood there out of sight of the foe that held them
   (round 27's tests). A unit walking its lanes near where it goes walks again (its walking speed: a
   march runs). In Spargus the Freedom League's units march at the Krimzon Guard unit nearest them
   (`bf-city-hunt`, round 55)."
  (let* ((w *bf-march*)
         (to (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
         (hunt? (and (= team BF_TEAM_FF) (bf-objective?)))
         (goal (if hunt?
                   (bf-city-hunt unit to)
                   (bf-city-unit-goal unit team)
                   )
               )
         )
    (if (and (not hunt?) (>= goal 0) (not (bf-city-zone-foe team goal (-> unit root trans) to)))
        (vector-copy! to (-> *bf* points goal pos))
        )
    ;; a unit with a foe in sight fights it (the stock guard's own attack), no march
    (when (and (-> unit nav) (bf-city-walking? unit) (not (bf-city-engaged? unit)))
      (cond
        ((and (>= goal 0) (< (-> w count) BF_MARCH_MAX) (-> w goal goal)
              (< BF_MARCH_NEAR (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) to))
              (bf-march-waypoint unit goal to (-> w to (-> w count)))
              )
         (set! (-> w unit (-> w count)) (process->handle unit))
         (set! (-> w from (-> w count)) (-> unit nav state mesh))
         (set! (-> w point (-> w count)) goal)
         ;; a bridge to cross at the waypoint: its code from the ways
         (let* ((k (bf-ways-index (-> unit nav state mesh)))
                (nx (if (>= k 0) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* goal BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -1))
                )
           (set! (-> w hop (-> w count)) (if (>= nx 100) nx -1))
           )
         (+! (-> w count) 1)
         )
        ;; no waypoint to its point: it runs its lanes there (`bf-city-choose-branch`), with no idle
        ;; stop; near its point, it walks them (round 42, the author's wish: units walked their
        ;; lanes as on patrol until a foe or a march made them run)
        ((and (>= goal 0) (< BF_MARCH_NEAR (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) to)))
         (set! (-> unit wait-time) (seconds 3600))
         (set! (-> unit nav target-speed) (* (-> unit speed-scale) (-> unit speed-run)))
         )
        (else
          (set! (-> unit nav target-speed) (* (-> unit speed-scale) (-> unit speed-walk)))
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-roll! ((unit citizen) (point int))
  "In `bf-march-apply`, every frame: robotguard UNIT marching to POINT rolls as a ball while it is
   farther than BF_ROLL_REACH from it, BF_ROLL_STOP once it rolls (the author's wish): its run clip,
   which the march's run plays (citizen-travel-anim, get-run-anim), becomes its ball, at
   BF_ROBOT_ROLL_SPEED, shown at once (its run blend full). Nearer, its stock run clip and the
   battle's run speed (`bf-city-unit-pace`)."
  (let* ((ball? (= (-> unit anim-run) BF_ROBOT_BALL_CLIP))
         (far? (and (>= point 0)
                    (< (if ball? BF_ROLL_STOP BF_ROLL_REACH)
                       (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> *bf* points point pos))
                       )
                    )
               )
         )
    (cond
      (far?
       (set! (-> unit speed-run) BF_ROBOT_ROLL_SPEED)
       (set! (-> unit dist-run-anim) BF_ROBOT_BALL_DIST)
       (when (not ball?)
         (set! (-> unit anim-run) BF_ROBOT_BALL_CLIP)
         (set! (-> unit interp) 1.0)
         (logior! (-> unit flags) (citizen-flag run-mode))
         (logclear! (-> unit flags) (citizen-flag shuffle-mode))
         )
       )
      (ball?
       (set! (-> unit anim-run) BF_ROBOT_RUN_CLIP)
       (bf-city-unit-pace unit)
       )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; A marching unit this close to its waypoint looks whether it already stands on its next mesh
;; (`bf-march-cross!`), that mesh's poly under it at most BF_CROSS_RISE above or below its feet
;; (2.5 m in round 47's first runs: units 2.8 and 3.3 m under a link poly's middle, on a slope, stood
;; for their stuck hop; the city's upper decks lie 8 m and more over its streets).
(defconstant BF_CROSS_REACH (meters 12))
(defconstant BF_CROSS_RISE (meters 4))

(defun bf-mesh-covers? ((m nav-mesh) (pos vector) (rise float))
  "#t when a poly of nav mesh M lies under POS: its outline holds POS across (`point-in-poly?`, in
   the mesh's own frame) and its middle is within RISE of POS's height."
  (let ((local (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) pos (the-as vector (-> m bounds))))
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
      (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
        (when (point-in-poly? m poly local)
          (poly-centroid m poly c)
          (if (< (fabs (- (-> c y) (-> pos y))) rise)
              (return #t)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-march-cross! ((unit citizen) (i int))
  "In `bf-march-apply`: marching unit UNIT (`*bf-march*` entry I), within BF_CROSS_REACH of the link
   it heads for, onto the mesh that link leads to as soon as it stands on that mesh's ground
   (`bf-mesh-covers?`). Jak 2's city meshes overlap where they link, a link poly inside the other
   mesh's ground: a unit coming from that side stood 3.5 to 5 m short of its waypoint (2 m past the
   link poly), never stepped on the link poly (nav-enemy-method-188 changes meshes there alone), and
   waited for its stuck hop, 63 times in a run at one link (round 47's tests). Standing there on the
   new mesh's own link poly back, the stock change of meshes sent it back at once: no link poly
   sends it back to the mesh it left for a second (battlefront.gc `bf-link-hold!`). Returns #t when
   it changed meshes: the next frame gives it its waypoint on the new one."
  (let* ((w *bf-march*)
         (m (-> unit nav state mesh))
         (pt (-> w point i))
         )
    (when (and m (>= pt 0) (< (-> w hop i) 100)
               (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> w to i)) BF_CROSS_REACH)
               )
      (let* ((k (bf-ways-index m))
             (nx (if (>= k 0) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* pt BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -1))
             )
        (when (and (>= nx 0) (< nx 100))
          (let ((dest (-> m link-array (bf-march-link m k pt (-> unit pid) nx) dest-mesh)))
            (when (and dest (!= dest m) (bf-mesh-covers? dest (-> unit root trans) BF_CROSS_RISE))
              (change-to dest unit)
              (when (= (-> unit nav state mesh) dest)
                ;; no link poly of its new mesh sends it back at once (battlefront.gc)
                (bf-link-hold! unit m)
                #t
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-march-apply ()
  "Every frame of the fight: each marching unit (`*bf-march*`), still walking its lanes (`bf-city-walking?`),
   runs to its waypoint: its controller's dest-point, which the citizen's 'active post gives its nav
   control as target each frame (citizen.gc), the nav control finding the way across the mesh. The
   lanes set it again at a lane's end; this puts it back the next frame. No idle stop on the way
   (wait-time: the 'active trans stops the unit once it is over). A unit that moved onto its next
   mesh goes on at once to its next waypoint there (left to its lanes until the next plan, a unit at
   the edge of a section turned back and circled)."
  (let ((w *bf-march*))
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (let ((unit (the-as citizen (handle->process (-> w unit i)))))
        (when (and unit (bf-city-walking? unit) (-> unit nav))
          (cond
            ((!= (-> unit nav state mesh) (-> w from i))
             ;; onto its next mesh: on at once to its next waypoint. Left to its lanes until the next
             ;; plan, a unit at the edge of a section turned back and circled there (the author's play)
             (let* ((pt (-> w point i))
                    (m (-> unit nav state mesh))
                    (k (if m (bf-ways-index m) -1))
                    (nx (if (>= k 0) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* pt BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -1))
                    )
               (cond
                 ((and m (>= pt 0) (bf-march-waypoint unit pt (-> *bf* points pt pos) (-> w to i)))
                  (set! (-> w from i) m)
                  (set! (-> w hop i) (if (>= nx 100) nx -1))
                  )
                 (else
                   (set! (-> w unit i) (the-as handle #f))
                   )
                 )
               )
             )
            ;; at a bridge's end: onto the other mesh, just across the seam
            ((and (>= (-> w hop i) 100)
                  (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> w to i)) BF_BRIDGE_HOP)
                  )
             (let* ((code (- (-> w hop i) 100))
                    (b (/ code 2))
                    (from-a? (zero? (logand code 1)))
                    (dest (-> *bf-ways* mesh (if from-a? (-> *bf-ways* mesh-b b) (-> *bf-ways* mesh-a b))))
                    )
               (change-to dest unit)
               (move-to-point! (-> unit root) (if from-a? (-> *bf-ways* end-b b) (-> *bf-ways* end-a b)))
               (set! (-> w unit i) (the-as handle #f))
               )
             )
            ;; standing on its next mesh's ground near the link: onto that mesh
            ((bf-march-cross! unit i)
             (+! (-> *bf-crossings* 0) 1)
             )
            ;; stuck BF_STUCK_HOP near its waypoint (a seam its nav does not cross: two units stood 55
            ;; and 90 s at (760, 1206), between the Port and the Industrial Zone, round 29's tests):
            ;; put onto the waypoint, on its mesh. Not on its point's own mesh: no seam to cross there,
            ;; it stands at its point (round 47: units 4 to 12 m from their point were put onto it)
            ((let ((k (logand (-> unit pid) (+ BF_GOAL_SLOTS -1))))
               (and (!= (-> unit nav state mesh) (-> w goal (-> w point i)))
                    (= (-> *bf-goals* unit k) (process->handle unit))
                    (< BF_STUCK_HOP (- (-> *display* game-clock frame-counter) (-> *bf-goals* time k)))
                    (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> w to i)) BF_STUCK_HOP_REACH)
                    )
               )
             (let ((dest (find-nearest-nav-mesh (-> w to i) (meters 4)))
                   (k (logand (-> unit pid) (+ BF_GOAL_SLOTS -1)))
                   )
               (when dest
                 (change-to dest unit)
                 (move-to-point! (-> unit root) (-> w to i))
                 (+! (-> *bf-stuck-hops* 0) 1)
                 (format 0 "battlefront: unit ~D stuck, put onto its waypoint at ~M ~M~%" (-> unit pid) (-> w to i x) (-> w to i z))
                 )
               (vector-copy! (-> *bf-goals* pos k) (-> unit root trans))
               (set! (-> *bf-goals* time k) (-> *display* game-clock frame-counter))
               )
             )
            (else
              (vector-copy! (-> unit dest-point) (-> w to i))
              (set! (-> unit wait-time) (seconds 3600))
              (if (= (-> unit type symbol) 'roboguard-city)
                  (bf-city-roll! unit (-> w point i))
                  )
              (set! (-> unit nav target-speed) (* (-> unit speed-scale) (-> unit speed-run)))
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-choose-branch ((ctrl vehicle-controller) (unit vehicle))
  "The lane a unit of the battle takes at the end of its lane (its controller's
   choose-branch-callback, `bf-city-steer`): the first lane of its way to its point
   (`bf-city-unit-goal`, `bf-city-route`). The lane graph joins every loaded section, so the unit
   finds its way across them; at its point it keeps turning back across it, where a capture counts
   it (within 20 m it used to wander at random, and its point's 15 m seldom held a defender). With
   no point, or marching over the meshes (`bf-marching?`: its waypoint, not a lane, leads it; the
   post asks for a lane every frame near it), the stock random lane (vehicle-controller method 15).
   #f, no lane, for a unit on none or on a lane leading out of the loaded graph: Spargus's few
   lanes (233, Haven City's 8955) left a guard out of a ship with no lane, whose guard code asked
   for the next one all the same, and the game crashed reading it (round 50's tests)."
  (let* ((proc (the-as process unit))
         (team (bf-unit-team proc))
         (br (-> ctrl branch))
         (goal (if (and (bf-fighting?) (>= team 0) (not (bf-marching? proc))) (bf-city-unit-goal proc team) -1))
         )
    (if (or (not br) (zero? br) (not (-> br dest-node)) (zero? (-> br dest-node)))
        (return (the-as nav-branch #f))
        )
    (if (< goal 0)
        (vehicle-controller-method-15 ctrl)
        (let ((first (bf-city-route (-> ctrl branch dest-node) (-> *bf* points goal pos))))
          (if first
              first
              (vehicle-controller-method-15 ctrl)
              )
          )
        )
    )
  )

(defconstant BF_LANE_REACH (meters 150)) ;; a unit on no lane takes the nearest within this

(defun bf-city-give-lane! ((unit citizen))
  "In `bf-city-steer`, twice a second: battle unit UNIT, on no lane, onto the pedestrian lane
   nearest it within BF_LANE_REACH (the stock search, `find-segment`, then citizen method 199, as
   its flight does within 20 m). Out of a ship far from Spargus's few lanes (233; Haven City's
   8955), a unit found none within the stock 20 m and stayed on none, and the guard code read its
   lane anyway (round 50's crashes: `bf-city-choose-branch`, flee-info method 13)."
  (let ((at (vector-copy! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> unit root trans))))
    (set! (-> at w) BF_LANE_REACH)
    (let ((seg (find-segment unit at (vector-z-quaternion! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> unit root quat)))))
      (if seg
          (citizen-method-199 unit seg)
          )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-unit-minimap ((proc process))
  "The game's minimap mark of unit PROC: a crimson-guard's, or a kg-squad-member's (flying turret,
   roboguard, spider robot). #f for none."
  (cond
    ((type? proc crimson-guard) (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) minimap))
    ((type? proc kg-squad-member) (-> (the-as kg-squad-member proc) minimap))
    (else (the-as connection-minimap #f))
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-robot-free ((unit citizen))
  "In `bf-city-steer`: robotguard UNIT of the battle, which sees foes within BF_ROBOT_SIGHT only
   (`bf-city-foe-ok?`), standing in its hostile states with no foe left ('hostile, 'hostile-stand,
   'reposition), walks its lanes again ('active, `go-process`): its focus kept it there, on a foe
   it no longer had. So does one rolling after no foe ('roll-chase): a robotguard falling from the
   sky as a ball lands in it (`bf-city-spawn-near`). A spider robot too, idle in its
   'wait-for-vulnerable or 'wait-for-vulnerable-close with no foe left: it leaves them only for a
   foe it has (spydroid.gc), and 95 of the round 45 census's units standing 30 s were spiders
   there (the author's report of stuck units)."
  (let ((info (-> unit attacker-info)))
    (when (and info (nonzero? info))
      (when (and (not (handle->process (-> info enemy)))
                 (-> unit next-state)
                 (let ((st (-> unit next-state name)))
                   (or (= st 'hostile) (= st 'hostile-stand) (= st 'reposition) (= st 'roll-chase)
                       (= st 'wait-for-vulnerable) (= st 'wait-for-vulnerable-close)
                       )
                   )
                 )
        (set! (-> unit focus handle) (the-as handle #f))
        (go-process unit (method-of-object unit active))
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-unit-stock-stride ((proc process))
  "For the tests: unit PROC's (a citizen) walk and run clips back to the ground the stock game gives
   them, its speeds kept: the stride before round 22, its legs as fast as its speed. Twice a second
   `bf-city-unit-pace` gives the round's back."
  (let ((k (bf-unit-kind proc))
        (unit (the-as citizen proc))
        )
    (when (>= k 0)
      (set! (-> unit dist-walk-anim) (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* (+ (* 4 k) 2)))
      (set! (-> unit dist-run-anim) (-> *bf-unit-stock-pace* (+ (* 4 k) 3)))
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-steer ()
  "Twice a second, each unit of the battle: its kind's pace times the stock speed
   (`bf-city-unit-pace`); away from its point it marches there over the nav meshes (`bf-march-plan`), and near it
   takes its lanes with `bf-city-choose-branch` (its controller's choose-branch-callback, the stock
   random pick otherwise), and fights what it meets on the way (the attack controller). The unit
   pools are rebuilt with the stock callbacks and speeds at each end of a battle (`initialize!`
   'life)."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (w *bf-march*)
        )
    (set! (-> w count) 0)
    (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
      (set! (-> w goal i) (find-nearest-nav-mesh (-> *bf* points i pos) (meters 2)))
      )
    ;; each side's units in each point's zone (`bf-city-contested-point`)
    (dotimes (k (* 2 BF_POINT_MAX))
      (set! (-> *bf-zone-near* k) 0)
      (set! (-> *bf-threat-near* k) 0)
      )
    (dotimes (d (-> *bf-unit-dots* count))
      (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
        (let ((dist (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> *bf-unit-dots* pos d) (-> *bf* points i pos)))
              (k (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX (-> *bf-unit-dots* team d)) i))
              )
          (if (< dist BF_ZONE_REACH)
              (+! (-> *bf-zone-near* k) 1)
              )
          (if (< dist BF_THREAT_REACH)
              (+! (-> *bf-threat-near* k) 1)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    ;; the ways to the points over every loaded mesh, built again every 10 s
    (if (or (zero? (-> *bf-ways* count)) (time-elapsed? (-> *bf-ways* time) (seconds 10)))
        (bf-ways-build)
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0))
                (when (type? proc citizen)
                  (bf-city-unit-pace proc)
                  ;; its foes: in sight, a robotguard's near (`bf-city-foe-ok?`)
                  (let ((info (-> (the-as citizen proc) attacker-info)))
                    (if (and info (nonzero? info) (!= (-> info callback) bf-city-foe-ok?))
                        (set! (-> info callback) bf-city-foe-ok?)
                        )
                    )
                  )
                ;; roboguard-city is CTYPESC's type, unknown here: told by its name (the spiders too)
                (if (or (= (-> proc type symbol) 'roboguard-city) (= (-> proc type symbol) 'spydroid))
                    (bf-city-robot-free (the-as citizen proc))
                    )
                )
              (when (and proc (type? proc citizen) (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0))
                (let ((ctrl (-> (the-as citizen proc) controller)))
                  (if (!= (-> ctrl choose-branch-callback) bf-city-choose-branch)
                      (set! (-> ctrl choose-branch-callback) bf-city-choose-branch)
                      )
                  (if (zero? (-> ctrl branch))
                      (bf-city-give-lane! (the-as citizen proc))
                      )
                  )
                (bf-march-plan (the-as citizen proc) (bf-unit-team proc))
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-sleep-all ()
  "As the fight starts: every unit of the battle awake goes back to its pool (`bf-transport-sleep`),
   so each side's units all come from its own ships, at its base first."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (n 0)
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          ;; from the end: a unit put to sleep leaves the list
          (countdown (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0))
                (deactivate-object tr (the-as int i) #t)
                (+! n 1)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (format 0 "battlefront: ~D units of the battle put back to sleep as the fight starts~%" n)
    )
  (none)
  )

;; The units drawn at once, at most (round 44): each one drawn writes about 6.5 KB into the frame's
;; global DMA buffer, which the engine never checks (display.gc, 2560 KB since round 43); a view of
;; 200 units filled 1.3 MB. The farthest from the camera past this many are hidden (no-draw-temp,
;; `bf-city-draw-cap`).
(defconstant BF_DRAW_MAX 240)
(defconstant BF_DRAW_STEP (meters 16)) ;; the distance's steps the cap counts the units by
(define *bf-draw-count* (new 'static 'array int32 64))

(defun bf-city-draw-cap ()
  "Every frame of the fight, after `bf-city-dots`: the units awake counted by their distance to the
   camera in steps of BF_DRAW_STEP, the nearest BF_DRAW_MAX drawn, the others hidden (no-draw-temp:
   the unit's own code never sets it, the draw skips it). Off a fight's end, the next battle's pools
   are new processes."
  (let ((dots *bf-unit-dots*)
        (cam (math-camera-pos))
        (cut 64)
        (sum 0)
        )
    (when (< BF_DRAW_MAX (-> dots count))
      (dotimes (k 64)
        (set! (-> *bf-draw-count* k) 0)
        )
      (dotimes (d (-> dots count))
        (+! (-> *bf-draw-count* (min 63 (the int (/ (vector-vector-distance (-> dots pos d) cam) BF_DRAW_STEP)))) 1)
        )
      (set! cut 0)
      (while (and (< cut 64) (< (+ sum (-> *bf-draw-count* cut)) BF_DRAW_MAX))
        (+! sum (-> *bf-draw-count* cut))
        (+! cut 1)
        )
      )
    ;; the units in steps below CUT drawn, the others hidden
    (let ((te *traffic-engine*))
      (when (and te (nonzero? te))
        (dotimes (ti 2)
          (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
            (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
              (let ((proc (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i)))))
                (when (and proc (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0) (nonzero? (-> proc draw)))
                  (if (< (the int (/ (vector-vector-distance (-> proc root trans) cam) BF_DRAW_STEP)) cut)
                      (logclear! (-> proc draw status) (draw-control-status no-draw-temp))
                      (logior! (-> proc draw status) (draw-control-status no-draw-temp))
                      )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-dots ()
  "Every frame of the fight: the units awake into `*bf-unit-dots*`, their places, headings and sides,
   for the maps (battlefront.gc `bf-draw-city-map`: the respawn page, R3, the START page), and each
   one's mark on the game's minimap in its side's color; the units awake of each kind
   (battlefront-h.gc `*bf-awake-kinds*`, round 44)."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (dots *bf-unit-dots*)
        )
    (set! (-> dots count) 0)
    (dotimes (k 4)
      (set! (-> *bf-awake-kinds* k) 0)
      )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i)))))
              (when (and proc (>= (bf-unit-team proc) 0) (< (-> dots count) BF_DOT_MAX))
                ;; its minimap mark in its side's color: the stock guard's blue one for the Freedom
                ;; League (class 25, guard-frustum), the stock robot's red one for the Krimzon Guard
                ;; (139, robot-frustum), where the stock gives the guard's to every crimson-guard
                ;; (the red guards too) and the robot's to every flying turret (the blue jetpacks
                ;; too); every frame, from the first one it is awake
                (let ((mm (bf-city-unit-minimap proc)))
                  (if mm
                      (set! (-> mm class) (-> *minimap-class-list* (if (= (bf-unit-team proc) BF_TEAM_FF) 25 139)))
                      )
                  )
                (let ((k (-> dots count)))
                  (vector-copy! (-> dots pos k) (-> proc root trans))
                  (set! (-> dots yaw k) (vector-y-angle (vector-z-quaternion! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> proc root quat))))
                  (set! (-> dots team k) (bf-unit-team proc))
                  (+! (-> dots count) 1)
                  )
                (let ((kind (bf-unit-kind proc)))
                  (if (>= kind 0)
                      (+! (-> *bf-awake-kinds* kind) 1)
                      )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-reach ((pt int))
  "Nav meshes with a way to point PT (`*bf-ways*`), for the tests; the meshes listed when PT is -1."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (n 0)
        )
    (if (< pt 0)
        (return (the-as int (-> w count)))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (if (!= (-> w next (+ (* pt BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -1)
          (+! n 1)
          )
      )
    n
    )
  )

(defun bf-ways-islands ()
  "For the tests: each nav mesh the ways know cut into its islands, the polys joined by their edges
   (`adj-poly`, 255 for none): each island's polys, link polys, height range of its polys' middles
   and its middle. An island with no link poly reaches no other mesh."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (isl (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int16 256))
        (queue (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int16 256))
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (sum (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let* ((m (-> w mesh k))
             (n (the-as int (-> m poly-count)))
             (count 0)
             )
        (dotimes (i n)
          (set! (-> isl i) -1)
          )
        (dotimes (i n)
          (when (< (-> isl i) 0)
            (let ((head 0)
                  (tail 1)
                  (polys 0)
                  (links 0)
                  (lo 1000000000.0)
                  (hi -1000000000.0)
                  )
              (vector-reset! sum)
              (set! (-> queue 0) i)
              (set! (-> isl i) count)
              (while (< head tail)
                (let ((poly (-> m poly-array (-> queue head))))
                  (+! head 1)
                  (+! polys 1)
                  (if (logtest? (-> poly pat) 4)
                      (+! links 1)
                      )
                  (poly-centroid m poly c)
                  (set! lo (fmin lo (-> c y)))
                  (set! hi (fmax hi (-> c y)))
                  (vector+! sum sum c)
                  (dotimes (e (-> poly vertex-count))
                    (let ((adj (-> poly adj-poly e)))
                      (when (and (!= adj 255) (< adj n) (< (-> isl adj) 0))
                        (set! (-> isl adj) count)
                        (set! (-> queue tail) (the-as int adj))
                        (+! tail 1)
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              (vector-float*! sum sum (/ 1.0 (the float polys)))
              (format 0 "SMOKE island mesh ~D #~D: ~D polys ~D links y ~M to ~M" k count polys links lo hi)
              (format 0 " at ~M ~M~%" (-> sum x) (-> sum z))
              (+! count 1)
              )
            )
          )
        (format 0 "SMOKE mesh ~D: ~D polys, ~D islands~%" k n count)
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-pats ((only int))
  "For the tests: each nav mesh's polys by type (`pat` bits: 1 a gap a walker jumps or does not
   cross, 2 a poly the walks avoid, 4 a link to another mesh, 8 the last kind), and for mesh ONLY
   (-1 none) each poly: its index, type, height and middle, and its neighbours with their types
   and heights."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (d (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let ((m (-> w mesh k))
            (n1 0)
            (n2 0)
            (n4 0)
            (n8 0)
            )
        (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
          (let ((pat (-> m poly-array i pat)))
            (if (logtest? pat 1) (+! n1 1))
            (if (logtest? pat 2) (+! n2 1))
            (if (logtest? pat 4) (+! n4 1))
            (if (logtest? pat 8) (+! n8 1))
            )
          )
        (format 0 "SMOKE pats mesh ~D: ~D polys, gap ~D, avoid ~D, link ~D, other ~D~%" k (-> m poly-count) n1 n2 n4 n8)
        (when (= k only)
          (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
            (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
              (poly-centroid m poly c)
              (format 0 "SMOKE poly ~D ~D: pat ~D y ~M at ~M ~M adj" k i (-> poly pat) (-> c y) (-> c x) (-> c z))
              (dotimes (e (-> poly vertex-count))
                (let ((adj (-> poly adj-poly e)))
                  (when (!= adj 255)
                    (poly-centroid m (-> m poly-array adj) d)
                    (format 0 " ~D/~D/~M" adj (-> m poly-array adj pat) (-> d y))
                    )
                  )
                )
              (format 0 "~%")
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define *bf-test-counts* (new 'static 'array int32 4 0 0 0 0))

(defun bf-city-test-counts ()
  "For the tests, into `*bf-test-counts*`: 0 the guards standing on an upper deck (`bf-deck-via`),
   1 the guards that have been on one (`*bf-deck-done*`), 2 the posted units within 20 m of their
   point while no unit of the other side is within BF_THREAT_REACH of it, 3 the posted units."
  (dotimes (i 4)
    (set! (-> *bf-test-counts* i) 0)
    )
  (dotimes (i BF_DECK_DONE_MAX)
    (if (handle->process (-> *bf-deck-done* unit i))
        (+! (-> *bf-test-counts* 1) 1)
        )
    )
  (iterate-process-tree
    *active-pool*
    (lambda ((p process))
      (when (and (type? p nav-enemy) (>= (bf-unit-team p) 0) (-> p next-state) (!= (-> p next-state name) 'inactive))
        (let* ((u (the-as nav-enemy p))
               (m (if (nonzero? (-> u nav)) (-> u nav state mesh)))
               (poly (if (nonzero? (-> u nav)) (-> u nav state current-poly)))
               (k (if m (bf-ways-index m) -1))
               (post (bf-post-point p))
               )
          (when (and (= (-> p type symbol) 'crimson-guard) m poly (>= k 0))
            (let ((c (poly-centroid m poly (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))))
              (if (< (-> *bf-ways* deck-y k) (-> c y))
                  (+! (-> *bf-test-counts* 0) 1)
                  )
              )
            )
          (when (>= post 0)
            (+! (-> *bf-test-counts* 3) 1)
            (if (and (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> u root trans) (-> *bf* points post pos)) (meters 20))
                     (zero? (-> *bf-threat-near* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX (bf-other-team (bf-unit-team p))) post)))
                     )
                (+! (-> *bf-test-counts* 2) 1)
                )
            )
          )
        )
      #t
      )
    *null-kernel-context*
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-unit-report ()
  "For the tests: each unit of the battle awake: its type, process id, side, state, place, goal
   point (`bf-city-unit-goal`) and how far, the way from its mesh to it (`*bf-ways*` next: -2 on
   the point's mesh, -1 none), its mesh's index, its march and fight, and how high it stands over
   its nav poly's middle (that middle lies 0.5 to 1.4 m under the street)."
  (iterate-process-tree
    *active-pool*
    (lambda ((p process))
      (when (and (type? p nav-enemy) (>= (bf-unit-team p) 0) (-> p next-state) (!= (-> p next-state name) 'inactive))
        (let* ((u (the-as nav-enemy p))
               (team (bf-unit-team p))
               (goal (bf-city-unit-goal p team))
               (nav? (and (nonzero? (-> u nav)) (-> u nav)))
               (m (if nav? (-> u nav state mesh)))
               (poly (if nav? (-> u nav state current-poly)))
               (k (if m (bf-ways-index m) -1))
               (way (if (and (>= goal 0) (>= k 0)) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* goal BF_WAY_MESHES) k)) -9))
               (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
               )
          (if (and m poly)
              (poly-centroid m poly c)
              (vector-copy! c (-> u root trans))
              )
          (format 0 "SMOKE unit ~A ~D side ~D ~A" (-> p type symbol) (-> p pid) team (-> p next-state name))
          (format 0 " at ~M ~M ~M" (-> u root trans x) (-> u root trans y) (-> u root trans z))
          (format 0 " goal ~D ~M way ~D mesh ~D" goal
                  (if (>= goal 0) (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> u root trans) (-> *bf* points goal pos)) -1.0) way k
                  )
          (format 0 " march ~A fight ~A over ~M~%" (bf-marching? p) (bf-city-engaged? p) (- (-> u root trans y) (-> c y)))
          )
        )
      #t
      )
    *null-kernel-context*
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-dump ()
  "Print every nav mesh the ways know: its level, center, radius and links (the index of each
   link's mesh, -1 for a mesh not loaded), for the tests."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*))
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let ((m (-> w mesh k))
            (lev-name #f)
            )
        (dotimes (li (-> *level* length))
          (let ((lev (-> *level* level li)))
            (when (= (-> lev status) 'active)
              (let ((meshes (-> lev bsp nav-meshes)))
                (when (nonzero? meshes)
                  (dotimes (i (-> meshes length))
                    (if (= (-> meshes i nav-mesh) m)
                        (set! lev-name (-> lev name))
                        )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        (format 0 "SMOKE mesh ~D ~A at ~M ~M r ~M polys ~D links:" k lev-name (-> m bounds x) (-> m bounds z) (-> m bounds r) (-> m poly-count))
        (dotimes (l (-> m link-count))
          (let ((d (-> m link-array l dest-mesh)))
            (format 0 " ~D" (if d (bf-ways-index d) -1))
            )
          )
        (format 0 "~%")
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-near ((pt vector) (reach float))
  "Print every nav poly of the loaded meshes (`*bf-ways*`) whose middle lies within REACH of PT
   across, the link polys aside: its mesh's index, its middle and how far, for the tests (where to
   put a control point)."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let ((m (-> w mesh k)))
        (when (and m (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (the-as vector (-> m bounds)) pt) (+ (-> m bounds r) reach)))
          (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
            (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
              (when (not (logtest? (-> poly pat) 4))
                (poly-centroid m poly c)
                (if (< (vector-vector-xz-distance c pt) reach)
                    (format 0 "SMOKE poly mesh ~D at ~M ~M ~M, ~M away~%" k (-> c x) (-> c y) (-> c z) (vector-vector-xz-distance c pt))
                    )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-bridge-report ()
  "For the tests: each bridge of `*bf-ways*` (its meshes and ends), then each unit of the battle
   awake within 30 m of one of its ends: its process id, side, state, mesh index, how far from each
   end, its march and the bridge it hops."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*))
    (dotimes (b (-> w bridge-count))
      (format 0 "SMOKE bridge ~D meshes ~D ~D a ~M ~M ~M" b (-> w mesh-a b) (-> w mesh-b b)
              (-> w end-a b x) (-> w end-a b y) (-> w end-a b z))
      (format 0 " b ~M ~M ~M~%" (-> w end-b b x) (-> w end-b b y) (-> w end-b b z))
      )
    )
  (iterate-process-tree
    *active-pool*
    (lambda ((p process))
      (when (and (type? p nav-enemy) (>= (bf-unit-team p) 0) (-> p next-state) (!= (-> p next-state name) 'inactive))
        (let ((u (the-as nav-enemy p))
              (w *bf-ways*)
              )
          (dotimes (b (-> w bridge-count))
            (let ((da (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> u root trans) (-> w end-a b)))
                  (db (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> u root trans) (-> w end-b b)))
                  (hop -1)
                  )
              (when (< (fmin da db) (meters 30))
                (dotimes (i (-> *bf-march* count))
                  (if (= (-> *bf-march* unit i) (process->handle p))
                      (set! hop (-> *bf-march* hop i))
                      )
                  )
                (format 0 "SMOKE near bridge ~D: ~A ~D side ~D ~A mesh ~D" b (-> p type symbol) (-> p pid) (bf-unit-team p)
                        (-> p next-state name)
                        (if (and (nonzero? (-> u nav)) (-> u nav state mesh)) (bf-ways-index (-> u nav state mesh)) -1))
                (format 0 " a ~M b ~M march ~A hop ~D" da db (bf-marching? p) hop)
                (format 0 " goal ~D at ~M ~M~%" (bf-city-unit-goal p (bf-unit-team p)) (-> u root trans x) (-> u root trans z))
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      #t
      )
    *null-kernel-context*
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-unit-kind-name ((p process))
  "For the tests: a unit's kind with its side: red-guard, blue-guard, red-jet, blue-jet, or its type."
  (let ((sym (-> p type symbol)))
    (cond
      ((= sym 'crimson-guard) (if (bf-red-guard? p) 'red-guard 'blue-guard))
      ((= sym 'flying-turret) (if (= (bf-unit-team p) BF_TEAM_FF) 'blue-jet 'red-jet))
      (else sym)
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-target-report ()
  "For the tests: each unit of the battle the attack controller holds, awake: its process id, kind,
   side, state, place, goal point and how far, its foe's kind and how far, the nearest unit of the
   other side within 40 m (kind, how far, in sight), its march and its fight."
  (when (bf-city-controller?)
    (let ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*))
      (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
        (let* ((info (-> ctrl attackers data i))
               (p (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> info proc))))
               )
          (when (and p (!= p *target*) (>= (bf-unit-team p) 0) (-> p next-state) (!= (-> p next-state name) 'inactive)
                     (logtest? (-> info flags) (city-attacker-info-flag cai0))
                     )
            (let* ((team (bf-unit-team p))
                   (foe (-> info enemy-index))
                   (fp (if (>= foe 0) (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data foe proc)))))
                   (goal (bf-city-unit-goal p team))
                   (near (the-as process-drawable #f))
                   (near-d (meters 40))
                   )
              (dotimes (j (-> ctrl attackers length))
                (let ((q (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data j proc)))))
                  (when (and q (!= q p) (>= (bf-unit-team q) 0) (!= (bf-unit-team q) team)
                             (not (focus-test? (the-as process-focusable q) dead inactive))
                             )
                    (let ((d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> q root trans) (-> p root trans))))
                      (when (< d near-d)
                        (set! near q)
                        (set! near-d d)
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              (format 0 "SMOKE tgt ~D ~A ~D ~A at ~M ~M" (-> p pid) (bf-unit-kind-name p) team (-> p next-state name)
                      (-> p root trans x) (-> p root trans z))
              (format 0 " goal ~D ~M foe ~A ~M" goal
                      (if (>= goal 0) (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> p root trans) (-> *bf* points goal pos)) -1.0)
                      (if fp (bf-unit-kind-name fp) '-)
                      (if fp (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> fp root trans) (-> p root trans)) -1.0))
              (format 0 " near ~A ~M sees ~A march ~A fight ~A~%" (if near (bf-unit-kind-name near) '-) (if near near-d -1.0)
                      (if near (bf-city-sees? p near) #f) (bf-marching? p) (bf-city-engaged? p))
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define *bf-stuck-shown* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0)) ;; for the tests: `bf-city-stuck-report` lines printed

(defun bf-city-stuck-report ((after time-frame) (most int))
  "For the tests: each marching unit (`*bf-march*`) that has not moved BF_STUCK_MOVE for AFTER, within
   BF_STUCK_HOP_REACH of its waypoint, up to MOST lines in all (`*bf-stuck-shown*`): its process id,
   kind, mesh, current poly (id, pat, link), place, waypoint and how far (across and up), its nav
   state's flags, then the link of its way (`bf-march-link`): the link poly's middle, the next mesh
   and its own link poly's middle, and the gap between the two."
  (let ((w *bf-march*))
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (let* ((unit (the-as citizen (handle->process (-> w unit i))))
             (k (if unit (logand (-> unit pid) (+ BF_GOAL_SLOTS -1)) 0))
             )
        (when (and unit
                   (< (-> *bf-stuck-shown* 0) most)
                   (-> unit nav)
                   (-> unit nav state mesh)
                   (= (-> *bf-goals* unit k) (process->handle unit))
                   (< after (- (-> *display* game-clock frame-counter) (-> *bf-goals* time k)))
                   (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> unit root trans) (-> w to i)) BF_STUCK_HOP_REACH)
                   )
          (+! (-> *bf-stuck-shown* 0) 1)
          (let* ((m (-> unit nav state mesh))
                 (mk (bf-ways-index m))
                 (poly (-> unit nav state current-poly))
                 (pt (-> w point i))
                 (nx (if (>= mk 0) (-> *bf-ways* next (+ (* pt BF_WAY_MESHES) mk)) -1))
                 (pos (-> unit root trans))
                 )
            (format 0 "SMOKE stuck ~D ~A mesh ~D poly ~D pat ~D link ~D" (-> unit pid) (bf-unit-kind-name unit) mk
                    (if poly (-> poly id) -1) (if poly (-> poly pat) -1) (if poly (-> poly link) -1))
            (format 0 " at ~M ~M ~M to ~M ~M ~M" (-> pos x) (-> pos y) (-> pos z) (-> w to i x) (-> w to i y) (-> w to i z))
            (format 0 " off ~M up ~M flags ~X next ~D hop ~D" (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> w to i)) (- (-> w to i y) (-> pos y))
                    (-> unit nav state flags) nx (-> w hop i))
            (when (and (>= mk 0) (>= nx 0) (< nx 100))
              (let* ((l (bf-march-link m mk pt (-> unit pid) nx))
                     (lk (-> m link-array l))
                     (dest (-> lk dest-mesh))
                     (a (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
                     (b (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
                     )
                (when (bf-march-link-poly m l a)
                  (format 0 " link ~D at ~M ~M ~M" l (-> a x) (-> a y) (-> a z))
                  (when (and dest (< (-> lk dest-link-poly-id) (-> dest poly-count)))
                    (poly-centroid dest (-> dest poly-array (-> lk dest-link-poly-id)) b)
                    (format 0 " into ~D at ~M ~M ~M gap ~M" (bf-ways-index dest) (-> b x) (-> b y) (-> b z) (vector-vector-distance a b))
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            (format 0 "~%")
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-ways-gap ((a int) (b int))
  "Print the two polys of meshes A and B (`*bf-ways*` indices) whose centroids are nearest, and
   their distance, for the tests."
  (let ((ma (-> *bf-ways* mesh a))
        (mb (-> *bf-ways* mesh b))
        (pa (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (pb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (best-a (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (best-b (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (best -1.0)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> ma poly-count))
      (poly-centroid ma (-> ma poly-array i) pa)
      (dotimes (j (-> mb poly-count))
        (poly-centroid mb (-> mb poly-array j) pb)
        (let ((d (vector-vector-distance pa pb)))
          (when (or (< best 0.0) (< d best))
            (set! best d)
            (vector-copy! best-a pa)
            (vector-copy! best-b pb)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (format 0 "SMOKE gap ~D-~D: ~M between ~M ~M ~M" a b best (-> best-a x) (-> best-a y) (-> best-a z))
    (format 0 " and ~M ~M ~M~%" (-> best-b x) (-> best-b y) (-> best-b z))
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-send ((team int) (pt int) (n int))
  "For the tests: N awake units of side TEAM moved onto battle point PT's nav mesh, around it within
   10 m (`change-to`, `move-to-point!`). Returns how many moved."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (mesh (find-nearest-nav-mesh (-> *bf* points pt pos) (meters 2)))
        (done 0)
        (at (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te) mesh)
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (< done n) (type? proc crimson-guard) (= (bf-unit-team proc) team) (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) nav))
                (vector-copy! at (-> *bf* points pt pos))
                (+! (-> at x) (* (meters 3) (the float (- (mod done 5) 2))))
                (+! (-> at z) (* (meters 3) (the float (- (/ done 5) 1))))
                (change-to mesh (the-as process-drawable proc))
                (move-to-point! (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) root) at)
                (+! done 1)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    done
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-march-count ((team int))
  "Units of side TEAM marching now (`*bf-march*`), for the tests."
  (let ((n 0)
        (w *bf-march*)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (let ((p (handle->process (-> w unit i))))
        (if (and p (= (bf-unit-team p) team))
            (+! n 1)
            )
        )
      )
    n
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-hidden-foes ()
  "For the tests: the battle's units with a foe now (the attack controller's), and how many of them
   have it behind a wall (`bf-city-sees?`): hidden times 1000 plus the units with a foe."
  (let ((all 0)
        (hidden 0)
        )
    (when (bf-city-controller?)
      (let ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*))
        (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
          (let* ((info (-> ctrl attackers data i))
                 (nf (-> info enemy-index))
                 )
            (when (and (logtest? (-> info flags) (city-attacker-info-flag cai0)) (>= nf 0)
                       (>= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) 0)
                       )
              (let ((me (handle->process (-> info proc)))
                    (them (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data nf proc)))
                    )
                (when (and me them (type? me process-drawable) (type? them process-drawable))
                  (+! all 1)
                  (if (not (bf-city-sees? (the-as process-drawable me) (the-as process-drawable them)))
                      (+! hidden 1)
                      )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (+ (* hidden 1000) all)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-own-side-foes ()
  "For the tests: the battle's units whose foe (the attack controller's) is a unit of their own side.
   Blue robotguards and spider robots registered as the Krimzon Guard's types until round 47: they
   and the blue guards fought each other at no damage, all battle long."
  (let ((n 0))
    (when (bf-city-controller?)
      (let ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*))
        (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
          (let* ((info (-> ctrl attackers data i))
                 (nf (-> info enemy-index))
                 )
            (when (and (logtest? (-> info flags) (city-attacker-info-flag cai0)) (>= nf 0))
              (let ((me (handle->process (-> info proc)))
                    (them (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data nf proc)))
                    )
                (if (and me them (>= (bf-unit-team me) 0) (= (bf-unit-team me) (bf-unit-team them)))
                    (+! n 1)
                    )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    n
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-guard-pace ((out vector))
  "For the tests: the first awake guard of the battle's run speed into OUT x and its run clip's
   ground into y (units; `bf-city-unit-pace`). Returns #t when there is one."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*))
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (type? proc crimson-guard))
                (set! (-> out x) (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) speed-run))
                (set! (-> out y) (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) dist-run-anim))
                (return #t)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-city-guard-speed ()
  "The fastest awake guard of the battle now, its nav speed (units a second), for the tests: a run
   at its pace (`*bf-unit-pace*`) times the stock 12 m/s reaches 25 m/s (18 m/s until round 33)."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (best 0.0)
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and proc (type? proc crimson-guard) (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) nav))
                (set! best (fmax best (-> (the-as crimson-guard proc) nav state speed)))
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    best
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-free-navs ()
  "Just before an `initialize!` 'life (a battle's start or end, a far respawn): every unit of the
   traffic's pools, asleep or awake, that holds a nav-control on the engine's `*default-nav-mesh*`
   gives it back (remove-process-drawable). A new unit takes one there (citizen.gc, its enemy
   info's nav mesh) until it is first woken onto a street's mesh, and the reset left the old pools'
   ones taken while the new pools took theirs: 41 of the 128 before a far respawn's reset, 115 a
   second after it, and a new guard's setup crashed the game on the next (nav-enemy setup-enemy!).
   The units go in the reset."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (n 0)
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ty 29)
        (let ((info (-> te object-type-info-array ty)))
          (dotimes (i (-> info inactive-count))
            (let ((proc (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> info array i)))))
              (when (and proc (nonzero? (-> proc nav)) (-> proc nav) (= (-> proc nav state mesh) *default-nav-mesh*))
                (remove-process-drawable *default-nav-mesh* proc)
                (+! n 1)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((proc (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i)))))
              (when (and proc (nonzero? (-> proc nav)) (-> proc nav) (= (-> proc nav state mesh) *default-nav-mesh*))
                (remove-process-drawable *default-nav-mesh* proc)
                (+! n 1)
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      (format 0 "battlefront: ~D units gave back the default nav mesh (~D of ~D now taken)~%" n
              (-> *default-nav-mesh* nav-control-count) (-> *default-nav-mesh* max-nav-control-count))
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The champions in the attack controller (round 49; round 53: one a side)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

;; Each champion's place in the attack controller (`bf-city-boss-attacker!`), #f for none: the other
;; side's units near him turn onto him (`bf-city-retarget`). The Krimzon Guard's, then the Freedom
;; League's.
(define *bf-city-boss-info* (the-as city-attacker-info #f))
(define *bf-city-boss-info-ff* (the-as city-attacker-info #f))

(defun bf-city-set-foe! ((ctrl mission-squad-control) (info city-attacker-info) (k int))
  "Attacker INFO's foe set to attacker K, as mission-squad-control-method-13 sets the one it picks:
   the old foe's count of attackers down one, K's up one."
  (when (!= k (-> info enemy-index))
    (if (>= (-> info enemy-index) 0)
        (+! (-> ctrl attackers data (-> info enemy-index) num-current-attackers) -1)
        )
    (logior! (-> info flags) (city-attacker-info-flag cai2))
    (set! (-> info enemy-index) k)
    (set! (-> info enemy) (-> ctrl attackers data k proc))
    (set! (-> info enemy-type) (-> ctrl attackers data k self-type))
    (+! (-> ctrl attackers data k num-current-attackers) 1)
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-boss-attacker! ((body process) (info structure) (team int))
  "Called by battlefront-baron.gc (GAME) for the body of side TEAM's champion (Baron Praxis, Ashelin):
   with INFO #f, a place in the attack controller for BODY as a unit of that side (type 9, a Krimzon
   Guard robotguard; type 4, a Freedom League rifle guard: the other side's units hate it and pick
   it as a foe), returned, #f when the controller has none left; with INFO, that place given back
   (its foes' foe cleared), #f returned."
  (cond
    ((zero? *cty-attack-controller*)
     (the-as structure #f)
     )
    (info
     (remove-attacker *cty-attack-controller* (the-as city-attacker-info info))
     (if (= team BF_TEAM_KG)
         (set! *bf-city-boss-info* #f)
         (set! *bf-city-boss-info-ff* #f)
         )
     (the-as structure #f)
     )
    (else
      (let ((a (allocate-attacker *cty-attack-controller*)))
        (if a
            (init! a body (if (= team BF_TEAM_KG) 9 4))
            )
        (if (= team BF_TEAM_KG)
            (set! *bf-city-boss-info* a)
            (set! *bf-city-boss-info-ff* a)
            )
        (the-as structure a)
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-boss-pull! ((ctrl mission-squad-control) (info city-attacker-info) (b city-attacker-info) (pos vector) (team int))
  "Attacker INFO at POS, a unit of side TEAM, turns onto champion B (the other side's, #f for none)
   when it stands within BF_ENGAGE_REACH of him, nearer him than its foe (`bf-city-retarget`)."
  (when (and b
             (= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) team)
             (>= (-> b self-index) 0)
             (!= (-> info enemy-index) (-> b self-index))
             )
    (let ((bd (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data (-> b self-index) pos)))
          (nf (-> info enemy-index))
          )
      (if (and (< bd BF_ENGAGE_REACH)
               (or (< nf 0) (< bd (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data nf pos))))
               )
          (bf-city-set-foe! ctrl info (-> b self-index))
          )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define *bf-city-artifact-info* (the-as city-attacker-info #f))

(defconstant BF_ARTIFACT_KEEP (meters 10)) ;; the Krimzon Guard's units over the pass attack the artifact unless their foe is this close
(defconstant BF_ARTIFACT_WEST (meters 1990)) ;; over the pass: west of this (the Freedom League's drops' limit too)
;; Round 54's tests: within 45 m, then 150 m of it, the Freedom League's defenders held the attackers
;; 130 m off and none of them ever fired at it (a Freedom League sent to meet them held them at the
;; pass instead); from anywhere on the map, they stood at the pass's east end (x 1977 m): a unit with
;; a foe chases it with its stock moves, which stop at the end of its nav mesh, and the march alone
;; crosses the pass (`bf-march-cross!`). So the attackers go for it once over the pass, in its
;; district, fighting only the foes at their feet.

(defun bf-city-artifact-attacker! ((body process) (info structure))
  "Called by battlefront-artifact.gc (GAME) for Spargus's precursor artifact (round 54): with INFO
   #f, a place in the attack controller for BODY as a unit of the Freedom League (type 4, a rifle
   guard: the Krimzon Guard's units hate it and pick it as a foe), returned, #f when the controller
   has none left; with INFO, that place given back, #f returned."
  (cond
    ((zero? *cty-attack-controller*)
     (the-as structure #f)
     )
    (info
     (remove-attacker *cty-attack-controller* (the-as city-attacker-info info))
     (set! *bf-city-artifact-info* #f)
     (the-as structure #f)
     )
    (else
      (let ((a (allocate-attacker *cty-attack-controller*)))
        (when a
          (init! a body 4)
          ;; its cache entry at once (mission-squad-control-method-12 fills it on its next pass): read
          ;; by `bf-city-retarget` the same frame, a new entry's place was a stale pointer (round 54's
          ;; test: access violation in vector-vector-xz-distance)
          (let ((c (-> *cty-attack-controller* attacker-cache data (-> a self-index))))
            (set! (-> c proc) body)
            (set! (-> c pos) (-> (the-as process-drawable body) root trans))
            (set! (-> c attackable?) #t)
            )
          )
        (set! *bf-city-artifact-info* a)
        (the-as structure a)
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-artifact-pull! ((ctrl mission-squad-control) (info city-attacker-info) (pos vector))
  "Attacker INFO at POS, a Krimzon Guard unit over the pass (west of BF_ARTIFACT_WEST, the artifact's
   district), turns onto it unless its foe stands within BF_ARTIFACT_KEEP of it (`bf-city-retarget`):
   the attackers go for the objective, fighting only the defenders at their feet."
  (let ((b *bf-city-artifact-info*))
    (when (and b
               (= (bf-ctt-team (-> info self-type)) BF_TEAM_KG)
               (>= (-> b self-index) 0)
               (!= (-> info enemy-index) (-> b self-index))
               )
      (let ((nf (-> info enemy-index)))
        (if (and (< (-> pos x) BF_ARTIFACT_WEST)
                 (or (< nf 0) (< BF_ARTIFACT_KEEP (vector-vector-xz-distance pos (-> ctrl attacker-cache data nf pos))))
                 )
            (bf-city-set-foe! ctrl info (-> b self-index))
            )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-nearest-poly ((pt vector) (out vector))
  "OUT: the middle of the nav poly of the loaded meshes (`*bf-ways*`) nearest PT, the link polys
   aside (Spargus's artifact stands on the ground the units walk, round 54). #f for none, else #t."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (best -1.0)
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let ((m (-> w mesh k)))
        (when m
          (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
            (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
              (when (not (logtest? (-> poly pat) 4))
                (poly-centroid m poly c)
                (let ((d (vector-vector-distance c pt)))
                  (when (or (< best 0.0) (< d best))
                    (set! best d)
                    (vector-copy! out c)
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (<= 0.0 best)
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-foes-of ((proc process))
  "For the tests: the attackers of the attack controller whose foe is PROC."
  (let ((n 0))
    (when (nonzero? *cty-attack-controller*)
      (let ((ctrl *cty-attack-controller*))
        (dotimes (i (-> ctrl attackers length))
          (if (= (handle->process (-> ctrl attackers data i enemy)) proc)
              (+! n 1)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    n
    )
  )

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Deaths out of view (round 48)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

;; A unit knocked to 0 hit points by another than Jak, out of view or over 110 m from the camera,
;; skips its death: enemy's knocked state (enemy-states.gc) sends it to die-fast at once. enemy's
;; die-fast does nothing, so a guard there stood frozen for good, deaf to every event, and stayed
;; in its side's count (round 47: no guard of either side died in 150 s). kg-squad-member's (the
;; robotguards', spiders' and jetpacks') goes inactive without a word to the traffic engine, so
;; their side lost nothing for them. During a battle both report the death (citizen
;; `cleanup-for-death`: 'child-killed to the traffic engine, whose set-process-to-killed calls
;; `bf-unit-killed`) and go inactive, as the protect missions' guards do (assault-enemies.gc).
;; roboguard-city, spydroid and flying-turret (CTYPESC, loaded after CWI) copy kg-squad-member's
;; state at their deftype.

;; A guard's die-fast. During a battle: its death reported, the guard inactive. Otherwise the stock
;; state (no enter, its code does nothing).
(defstate die-fast (crimson-guard)
  :virtual #t
  :enter (behavior ()
    (if (bf-active?)
        (cleanup-for-death self)
        )
    )
  )

;; A robotguard's, spider's or jetpack's die-fast. During a battle: its death reported, the unit
;; inactive. Otherwise inactive at once, as the stock state.
(defstate die-fast (kg-squad-member)
  :virtual #t
  :enter (behavior ()
    (if (bf-active?)
        (cleanup-for-death self)
        (go-inactive self)
        )
    )
  )

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Force fields: the ruins of the old town and the Metal Head nest closed (round 19)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

;; ctywide-obs.o comes after this file in CWI
(define-extern spawn-security-wall (function process vector vector float symbol handle))

(defconstant BF_FIELD_COUNT 2)

;; Each force field's ends, world x, y and z in meters, and its height. The ruins' is the game's own
;; security-wall-12 (ctyslumb), the street from Freedom HQ's district into the ruins (ctygenb), which
;; the game drops after its first task; the nest's crosses the street from the Port to the Metal
;; Head nest (mhcitya), just short of its dark eco door (mhcity-dark-eco-door-1, -381 m, 1199 m),
;; read off the START menu's map.
(define *bf-field-ends* (new 'static 'array float 14
                          389.75 7.94 -18.44 389.75 7.94 -70.72 40.0
                          -410.0 7.0 1212.0 -335.0 7.0 1212.0 40.0
                          )
        )

(deftype bf-city-fields (structure)
  "The force fields' walls (security-wall-child processes, children of the director)."
  ((wall  handle BF_FIELD_COUNT)
   )
  )

(define *bf-city-fields* (new 'static 'bf-city-fields))

(dotimes (i BF_FIELD_COUNT)
  (set! (-> *bf-city-fields* wall i) (the-as handle #f))
  )

(defun bf-city-fields-up ()
  "Twice a second in a fight: each force field's wall (`*bf-field-ends*`) spawned again when it is
   gone (a battle's start, a far respawn's reset): `spawn-security-wall` (ctywide-obs.gc), solid to
   Jak and drawn red wherever ctywide is loaded."
  (let ((parent (handle->process (-> *bf* director)))
        (a (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (b (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    ;; Jak 3's city only: its walls are its own places, and spawn-security-wall is its ctywide-obs.o,
    ;; which the ported war zones' DGOs leave out (Jak 2's city, Spargus)
    (when (and parent (not (bf-zone-ported? (-> *bf* zone))))
      (dotimes (i BF_FIELD_COUNT)
        (when (not (handle->process (-> *bf-city-fields* wall i)))
          (let ((e (* i 7)))
            (set-vector! a (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* e)) (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 1)))
                         (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 2))) 1.0)
            (set-vector! b (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 3))) (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 4)))
                         (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 5))) 1.0)
            (set! (-> *bf-city-fields* wall i)
                  (spawn-security-wall parent a b (meters (-> *bf-field-ends* (+ e 6))) #f)
                  )
            (format 0 "battlefront: force field ~D up~%" i)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-fields-down ()
  "Every force field's wall gone (the battle's end, a far respawn's reset)."
  (dotimes (i BF_FIELD_COUNT)
    (let ((wall (handle->process (-> *bf-city-fields* wall i))))
      (if wall
          (deactivate wall)
          )
      (set! (-> *bf-city-fields* wall i) (the-as handle #f))
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Reinforcements from the edge, as Star Wars Battlefront's command posts (round 19)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defconstant BF_EDGE_MIN (meters 60)) ;; an edge spawn stands at least this far from the player
(defconstant BF_EDGE_MAX (meters 220)) ;; and at most this far: its street's nav mesh and ground loaded
(define *bf-edge-min* BF_EDGE_MIN)     ;; the distance the current search asks for

(defun bf-city-branch-level ((branch nav-branch))
  "The active city section whose nav graph holds BRANCH (`bf-city-zone-branch?`), #f for none."
  (let ((addr (the-as uint branch)))
    (dotimes (i (-> *level* length))
      (let ((lev (-> *level* level i)))
        (when (and (= (-> lev status) 'active) (nonzero? (-> lev bsp)) (nonzero? (-> lev bsp city-level-info)))
          (let ((graph (-> lev bsp city-level-info nav-graph)))
            (if (and (nonzero? graph)
                     (>= addr (the-as uint (-> graph branch-array 0)))
                     (< addr (the-as uint (-> graph branch-array (-> graph branch-count))))
                     )
                (return lev)
                )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (the-as level #f)
  )

(defun bf-city-edge-segment ((found traffic-find-segment-struct) (seg nav-segment))
  "Callback of `bf-city-edge-spawn`'s search: keep the pedestrian segment the traffic could fill now
   (the stock spawn's tests, as the old reinforcements), in a loaded section other than the closed
   ruins and nest (ctygenb, mhcitya, mhcityb), its nav mesh loaded, `*bf-edge-min*` to BF_EDGE_MAX
   from the player: the one furthest along `found` dir (the way to the side's territory), give or
   take 20 m at random. A segment 540 m off had no nav mesh loaded: the traffic woke its unit
   without one (traffic-engine.gc activate-by-type, `get-nav-mesh` #f), the unit found no ground and
   kept its default nav mesh's nav-control, and the next reset overflowed that mesh (a crash)."
  (let ((lev (bf-city-branch-level (-> seg branch))))
    (when (and lev *target*
               (nonzero? (-> seg nav-mesh-id))
               (not (or (= (-> lev name) 'ctygenb) (= (-> lev name) 'mhcitya) (= (-> lev name) 'mhcityb)))
               (< (-> seg branch density) (the-as uint 128))
               (not (can-dest-be-used? *traffic-engine* (-> seg branch)))
               (< *bf-edge-min* (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> seg vertex 0) (-> *target* control trans)))
               (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> seg vertex 0) (-> *target* control trans)) BF_EDGE_MAX)
               (get-nav-mesh (the-as actor-id (-> seg nav-mesh-id)))
               )
      (let* ((d (vector-! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> seg vertex 0) (-> *target* control trans)))
             (rating (+ (vector-dot d (-> found dir)) (* (rand-vu) (meters 20))))
             )
        (when (or (not (-> found best-seg)) (< (-> found best-rating) rating))
          (set! (-> found best-rating) rating)
          (set! (-> found best-seg) seg)
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-team-live? ((team int))
  "#t when side TEAM holds a point in a loaded section (battlefront.gc `bf-point-live?`): its ship
   stationed there brings its units (bf-transport.gc)."
  (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
    (let ((pt (-> *bf* points i)))
      (if (and (= (-> pt owner) team) (bf-point-live? pt))
          (return #t)
          )
      )
    )
  #f
  )

(defun bf-city-edge-spawn ()
  "Twice a second in a fight: a side that holds no point in the loaded sections still fights here,
   as Star Wars Battlefront's armies come from every command post: one of its units a tick, of the
   kind it lacks most against its caps (bf-transport.gc `bf-transport-next-kind`, which puts one
   of its side's sleeping units first in the pool), comes in on a street of the loaded area's edge
   toward its nearest held point, 60 to 220 m from the player (from 30 m when none is that far),
   and marches on its point. A side with a point here gets its units from its ship there."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*))
    (when (and te (nonzero? te) *target* (bf-fighting?))
      (dotimes (team 2)
        (when (not (bf-city-team-live? team))
          (let ((kind (bf-transport-next-kind team)))
            (when (>= kind 0)
              (let ((found (new 'stack-no-clear 'traffic-find-segment-struct))
                    (near -1)
                    (near-d 0.0)
                    (info (-> te object-type-info-array kind))
                    )
                ;; the way to its territory: its held point nearest the player
                (dotimes (i (-> *bf* point-count))
                  (when (= (-> *bf* points i owner) team)
                    (let ((d (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> *bf* points i pos) (-> *target* control trans))))
                      (when (or (< near 0) (< d near-d))
                        (set! near i)
                        (set! near-d d)
                        )
                      )
                    )
                  )
                (when (>= near 0)
                  (vector-! (-> found dir) (-> *bf* points near pos) (-> *target* control trans))
                  (set! (-> found dir y) 0.0)
                  (vector-normalize! (-> found dir) 1.0)
                  (let ((before (-> info active-count)))
                    (dotimes (pass 2)
                      (when (= (-> info active-count) before)
                        (set! *bf-edge-min* (if (zero? pass) BF_EDGE_MIN (meters 30)))
                        (set! (-> found best-seg) #f)
                        (set! (-> found best-rating) 0.0)
                        (let ((sphere (vector-copy! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> *target* control trans))))
                          (set! (-> sphere w) (meters 600))
                          (callback-on-nav-segments-in-sphere te sphere 1 found bf-city-edge-segment)
                          )
                        (if (-> found best-seg)
                            (activate-by-type (-> te tracker1) (the-as traffic-type kind) (-> found best-seg) 0.0)
                            )
                        )
                      )
                    (if (!= (-> info active-count) before)
                        (format 0 "battlefront: side ~D unit came in at the edge, ~M from the player~%" team
                                (vector-vector-xz-distance (-> found best-seg vertex 0) (-> *target* control trans)))
                        )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defconstant BF_SPAWN_REACH (meters 250))  ;; units appear on the nav meshes this close to their control point (45 m until round 26, 90 m until round 27)
(defconstant BF_RESPAWN_REACH (meters 90)) ;; the player comes down from the sky this close to the point he picked

;; When each side may bring units in at a control point again (`bf-city-spawn-tick`).
(define *bf-spawn-time* (new 'static 'array time-frame 2))

;; Spargus's objective (round 54): the drops of a side anywhere on the map (`bf-city-spawn-spot` PT
;; #f) keep to x between these (its district: the Freedom League's west of the pass, wascityb with
;; the precursor game, the Krimzon Guard's east of it, wascitya). Set by `bf-city-spawn-tick`.
(define *bf-spawn-x* (new 'static 'array float 2 -1000000000.0 1000000000.0))
(defconstant BF_SPARGUS_FF_EAST (meters 1990))  ;; the Freedom League's drops west of this
(defconstant BF_SPARGUS_KG_WEST (meters 2110))  ;; the Krimzon Guard's east of this (the pass, 2078 m, between)

(defun bf-city-spawn-spot ((pt vector) (out vector) (reach float) (low? symbol))
  "OUT: the middle of a nav poly drawn at random among those of the loaded meshes (`*bf-ways*`)
   within REACH of PT across and 20 m up or down (PT #f: anywhere, REACH unused; Spargus's drops,
   round 52), the link polys aside: a street, a platform; LOW?:
   no poly of an upper deck (`*bf-ways*` deck-y, the Industrial Zone's walkways): a jetpack guard
   brought down there stayed stuck on them (the author's play, round 27). Returns its mesh, #f for
   none.
   The units come down within BF_SPAWN_REACH of their point (the author's wish, round 28: the
   fights spread over the city), the player within BF_RESPAWN_REACH of the point he picked."
  (let ((w *bf-ways*)
        (n 0)
        (found (the-as nav-mesh #f))
        (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (dotimes (k (-> w count))
      (let ((m (-> w mesh k)))
        (when (and m (or (not pt) (< (vector-vector-xz-distance (the-as vector (-> m bounds)) pt) (+ (-> m bounds r) reach))))
          (dotimes (i (-> m poly-count))
            (let ((poly (-> m poly-array i)))
              (when (not (logtest? (-> poly pat) 4))
                (poly-centroid m poly c)
                (when (and (or (and (not pt) (< (-> *bf-spawn-x* 0) (-> c x)) (< (-> c x) (-> *bf-spawn-x* 1)))
                               (and pt (< (vector-vector-xz-distance c pt) reach) (< (fabs (- (-> c y) (-> pt y))) (meters 20)))
                               )
                           (or (not low?) (< (-> c y) (-> w deck-y k)))
                           )
                  (+! n 1)
                  (when (zero? (rand-vu-int-count n))
                    (vector-copy! out c)
                    (set! found m)
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    found
    )
  )

;; The guards and jetpacks woken at a control point wait for their first frame awake before they go
;; up (`bf-city-sky-tick`): an event sent to a unit just woken reaches its sleeping state, and a
;; guard sent the 'jump at once stayed in the air, still walking.
(defconstant BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX 64) ;; 16 until round 45: past them a falling unit went untracked
(defconstant BF_SKY_JET_MAX (meters 15)) ;; a jetpack goes up this far at most: its flight holds it 18 m above the ground at most

(deftype bf-sky-wait (structure)
  ((count   int32)
   (unit    handle BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   (ground  vector BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX :inline)
   (height  float  BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   (frames  int32  BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   )
  )

(define *bf-sky-wait* (new 'static 'bf-sky-wait))

;; The robotguards and spiders falling from the sky (exit-transport, enemy-falling-post) meet the
;; scenery only, their collision kept here until they leave that state (`bf-city-sky-tick`): they
;; landed on the jetpacks hovering over the point (2 spiders in 8 stayed 12 m up).
(deftype bf-sky-fall (structure)
  ((count   int32)
   (unit    handle       BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   (collide collide-spec BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   (frames  int32        BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
   (ground  float        BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)   ;; the height of the nav poly it falls onto
   )
  )

(defconstant BF_FALL_FREE (meters 3)) ;; a unit falls through everything until this high over its nav poly

(define *bf-sky-fall* (new 'static 'bf-sky-fall))

(defconstant BF_FLOOR_ABOVE (meters 4)) ;; the floor a falling unit lands on lies at most this far over its nav poly's middle

(defun bf-city-floor ((pos vector) (ground float))
  "The floor under POS's place across: a probe of the scenery from BF_FLOOR_ABOVE over GROUND (a nav
   poly's middle) down to as far under it. A poly's middle lies under the floor (up to 1.4 m in the
   streets, meters on a stair: the Palace HQ of Jak 2's city), and a unit falling through
   everything got its collision back only BF_FALL_FREE over the middle: already under the floor,
   which has no underside, it fell 6 km under the city (the author's report of stuck units, round
   45). Higher scenery (pipes, walkways) is left out, as it should be. Returns GROUND when the probe
   meets nothing."
  (let ((cq (new 'stack-no-clear 'collide-query)))
    (set-vector! (-> cq start-pos) (-> pos x) (+ ground BF_FLOOR_ABOVE) (-> pos z) 1.0)
    (set-vector! (-> cq move-dist) 0.0 (* -2.0 BF_FLOOR_ABOVE) 0.0 1.0)
    (set! (-> cq radius) (meters 0.4))
    (set! (-> cq collide-with) (collide-spec backgnd))
    (set! (-> cq ignore-process0) #f)
    (set! (-> cq ignore-process1) #f)
    (set! (-> cq ignore-pat) (new 'static 'pat-surface :noentity #x1 :nojak #x1 :probe #x1 :noendlessfall #x1 :board #x1))
    (set! (-> cq action-mask) (collide-action solid))
    (let ((u (fill-and-probe-using-line-sphere *collide-cache* cq)))
      (if (>= u 0.0)
          (- (+ ground BF_FLOOR_ABOVE) (* u 2.0 BF_FLOOR_ABOVE))
          ground
          )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-fall-through! ((proc process) (ground float))
  "A robotguard or a spider robot falling from the sky or out of a ship's hatch (exit-transport,
   enemy-falling-post) onto a nav poly at height GROUND meets nothing until BF_FALL_FREE over the
   floor there (`bf-city-floor`), then the scenery only, until it leaves that state
   (`*bf-sky-fall*`, `bf-city-sky-tick`): over a control point they landed on the jetpacks hovering
   there; under the Krimzon Guard's ship, at its base, the spiders met the scenery 13 and 22 m up (6
   m and 14 m over the street), stood there and walked in the air (the author's play and the tests,
   round 26)."
  (set! ground (bf-city-floor (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root trans) ground))
  (when (< (-> *bf-sky-fall* count) BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX)
    (let ((n (-> *bf-sky-fall* count))
          (cs (the-as collide-shape (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root)))
          )
      (set! (-> *bf-sky-fall* unit n) (process->handle proc))
      (set! (-> *bf-sky-fall* collide n) (-> cs root-prim prim-core collide-with))
      (set! (-> *bf-sky-fall* frames n) 0)
      (set! (-> *bf-sky-fall* ground n) ground)
      (set! (-> cs root-prim prim-core collide-with)
            (if (< (+ ground BF_FALL_FREE) (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) root trans y))
                (the-as collide-spec 0)
                (collide-spec backgnd)
                )
            )
      (+! (-> *bf-sky-fall* count) 1)
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define-extern bf-city-land! (function nav-enemy float collide-spec none))

(defun bf-city-sky-tick ()
  "Every frame of the fight: each unit waiting to go up (`*bf-sky-wait*`), once in its 'active (its
   first frame awake), shows and goes up its height above its poly: a guard is sent the stock 'jump
   onto the poly (its landing is the stock guard's out of a ship), a jetpack flies down from
   BF_SKY_JET_MAX at most. A unit not 'active within 10 frames shows where it is. Each robotguard
   or spider falling (`*bf-sky-fall*`) gets its collision back once out of its exit-transport (10 s
   at most)."
  (let ((w *bf-sky-wait*)
        (n 0)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> w count))
      (let ((p (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> w unit i)))))
        (when p
          (cond
            ((and (-> p next-state) (= (-> p next-state name) 'active))
             (logclear! (-> p draw status) (draw-control-status no-draw))
             (cond
               ((= (-> p type symbol) 'crimson-guard)
                (+! (-> p root trans y) (-> w height i))
                (send-event p 'jump 0 (-> w ground i))
                )
               (else
                 (+! (-> p root trans y) (fmin (-> w height i) BF_SKY_JET_MAX))
                 )
               )
             )
            ((< (-> w frames i) 10)
             (when (!= n i)
               (set! (-> w unit n) (-> w unit i))
               (vector-copy! (-> w ground n) (-> w ground i))
               (set! (-> w height n) (-> w height i))
               (set! (-> w frames n) (-> w frames i))
               )
             (+! (-> w frames n) 1)
             (+! n 1)
             )
            (else
              (logclear! (-> p draw status) (draw-control-status no-draw))
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (set! (-> w count) n)
    )
  (let ((f *bf-sky-fall*)
        (n 0)
        )
    (dotimes (i (-> f count))
      (let ((p (the-as process-drawable (handle->process (-> f unit i)))))
        (when p
          (cond
            ((and (< (-> f frames i) 600)
                  (or (< (-> f frames i) 2) (and (-> p next-state) (= (-> p next-state name) 'exit-transport)))
                  )
             ;; BF_FALL_FREE over its poly: the scenery again, to land on the street
             (let ((cs (the-as collide-shape (-> p root))))
               (if (and (zero? (-> cs root-prim prim-core collide-with))
                        (< (-> p root trans y) (+ (-> f ground i) BF_FALL_FREE))
                        )
                   (set! (-> cs root-prim prim-core collide-with) (collide-spec backgnd))
                   )
               ;; past its floor with no scenery to stop it: landed there (`bf-city-land!`)
               (when (and (-> p next-state) (= (-> p next-state name) 'exit-transport)
                          (< (-> p root trans y) (- (-> f ground i) (meters 1)))
                          )
                 (bf-city-land! (the-as nav-enemy p) (-> f ground i) (-> f collide i))
                 (set! (-> f frames i) 600)
                 )
               )
             (when (!= n i)
               (set! (-> f unit n) (-> f unit i))
               (set! (-> f collide n) (-> f collide i))
               (set! (-> f frames n) (-> f frames i))
               (set! (-> f ground n) (-> f ground i))
               )
             (+! (-> f frames n) 1)
             (+! n 1)
             )
            (else
              (set! (-> (the-as collide-shape (-> p root)) root-prim prim-core collide-with) (-> f collide i))
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (set! (-> f count) n)
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-spawn-near ((team int) (point int))
  "Up to BF_TRANSPORT_BURST units of side TEAM, each of the kind it lacks most
   (`bf-transport-next-kind`), over a nav poly drawn at random around control point POINT
   (`bf-city-spawn-spot`): the author wanted no ship there, the units anywhere on the meshes near
   the point, platforms too, coming down from the sky with their landing (round 25), from
   `bf-sky-height` above the poly (of up to 3 drawn, the first with 6 m of sky over it). A guard or a jetpack is woken walking or flying ('active, traffic
   behavior 2) on the poly, hidden, and goes up on its first frame awake (`bf-city-sky-tick`): the
   guard then jumps onto the poly, the jetpack flies down. A robotguard and a spider are woken in
   their way out of a ship (behavior 6, exit-transport, which needs no ship), up there: the
   robotguard falls as a ball, the spider tumbling (its jump has no clips: a 'jump would read none).
   One in four is posted on the point; each is logged for the tests (`*bf-sky-log*`). POINT -1:
   anywhere on the map's meshes, none posted (Spargus, `bf-city-spawn-tick`). Returns how many
   came."
  (let ((done 0))
    (dotimes (k BF_TRANSPORT_BURST)
      (when (= k done)
        (let* ((kind (bf-transport-next-kind team))
               (at (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
               (sky (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
               ;; a jetpack guard never over the walkways (`bf-city-spawn-spot` LOW?)
               (low? (= kind (the-as int (traffic-type flying-turret))))
               (around (if (>= point 0) (-> *bf* points point pos) (the-as vector #f)))
               (mesh (if (>= kind 0) (bf-city-spawn-spot around at BF_SPAWN_REACH low?)))
               (h (if mesh (bf-sky-height at) 0.0))
               )
          ;; up to 3 polys drawn for one under the open sky
          (dotimes (try 2)
            (when (and mesh (< h (meters 6)))
              (let ((m2 (bf-city-spawn-spot around sky BF_SPAWN_REACH low?)))
                (when m2
                  (let ((h2 (bf-sky-height sky)))
                    (when (< h h2)
                      (set! mesh m2)
                      (set! h h2)
                      (vector-copy! at sky)
                      )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          (set! *bf-wake-kind* kind)
          (when (and mesh *traffic-manager* (bf-transport-mesh-room? mesh kind))
            (let ((params (new 'stack 'traffic-object-spawn-params))
                  (guard? (= kind (the-as int (traffic-type guard-a))))
                  )
              (vector-copy! sky at)
              (+! (-> sky y) h)
              (set! (-> params proc) #f)
              (set! (-> params object-type) (the-as traffic-type kind))
              (set! (-> params behavior)
                    (the-as uint (if (or (= kind (the-as int (traffic-type roboguard))) (= kind (the-as int (traffic-type spydroid))))
                                     6
                                     2
                                     )
                            )
                    )
              (set! (-> params id) (the-as uint 0))
              (set! (-> params nav-mesh) mesh)
              (set! (-> params nav-branch) #f)
              (set! (-> params handle) (the-as handle #f))
              (set! (-> params handle-parent) (the-as handle #f))
              (set! (-> params user-data) (the-as uint 0))
              (set! (-> params flags) (traffic-spawn-flags))
              (set! (-> params guard-type) (the-as uint 11))
              (set! (-> params entity) #f)
              (vector-reset! (-> params velocity))
              (vector-copy! (-> params position) (if (= (-> params behavior) 6) sky at))
              (quaternion-axis-angle! (-> params rotation) 0.0 1.0 0.0 (* 65536.0 (rand-vu)))
              (send-event *traffic-manager* 'activate-object params)
              (let ((proc (-> params proc)))
                (when proc
                  ;; a guard or a jetpack goes up on its first frame awake (`bf-city-sky-tick`),
                  ;; hidden until then
                  (when (and (not (= (-> params behavior) 6)) (< (-> *bf-sky-wait* count) BF_SKY_WAIT_MAX))
                    (let ((n (-> *bf-sky-wait* count)))
                      (set! (-> *bf-sky-wait* unit n) (process->handle proc))
                      (vector-copy! (-> *bf-sky-wait* ground n) at)
                      (set! (-> *bf-sky-wait* height n) h)
                      (set! (-> *bf-sky-wait* frames n) 0)
                      (+! (-> *bf-sky-wait* count) 1)
                      )
                    (logior! (-> (the-as process-drawable proc) draw status) (draw-control-status no-draw))
                    )
                  ;; a robotguard or a spider falls through the units (`bf-city-fall-through!`)
                  (if (= (-> params behavior) 6)
                      (bf-city-fall-through! proc (-> at y))
                      )
                  (let ((n (mod (-> *bf-sky-log* count) BF_SKY_LOG)))
                    (set! (-> *bf-sky-log* unit n) (process->handle proc))
                    (set! (-> *bf-sky-log* kind n) kind)
                    (vector-copy! (-> *bf-sky-log* ground n) at)
                    (set! (-> *bf-sky-log* height n) h)
                    (+! (-> *bf-sky-log* count) 1)
                    )
                  ;; its lanes' goal on itself until its march sends it on (`bf-march-apply`)
                  (if (type? proc citizen)
                      (vector-copy! (-> (the-as citizen proc) dest-point) at)
                      )
                  ;; one unit in four guards the point (bf-transport.gc `bf-post-set!`)
                  (bf-post-set! proc (if (and (>= point 0) (zero? (rand-vu-int-count 4))) point -1))
                  (if (>= point 0)
                      (+! (-> *bf-drops-at* (+ (* BF_POINT_MAX team) point)) 1)
                      )
                  (bf-unit-brought! team)
                  (+! done 1)
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    (if (> done (-> *bf-burst-max* 0))
        (set! (-> *bf-burst-max* 0) done)
        )
    done
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-spawn-tick ()
  "Twice a second in a fight, for each side whose next units come down at a control point
   (bf-transport.gc `bf-transport-drop-point`; at its base its ship brings them): `bf-city-spawn-near`,
   then the next units a second later, half a second after none (the point passed over once, as a
   ship's).
   In Spargus every unit comes down anywhere in its side's district instead (`bf-city-spawn-near`,
   point -1, `*bf-spawn-x*`), its ships bringing none (bf-transport.gc `bf-transport-my-turn?`): the
   Freedom League's west of the pass, where the precursor game and the artifact it defends stand,
   the Krimzon Guard's east of it (the author's wish, round 54; round 52 dropped both anywhere)."
  (dotimes (team 2)
    (when (and (= (-> *bf* zone) BF_ZONE_SPARGUS) (>= (current-time) (-> *bf-spawn-time* team)))
      (set! (-> *bf-spawn-x* 0) (if (= team BF_TEAM_FF) -1000000000.0 BF_SPARGUS_KG_WEST))
      (set! (-> *bf-spawn-x* 1) (if (= team BF_TEAM_FF) BF_SPARGUS_FF_EAST 1000000000.0))
      (set! (-> *bf-spawn-time* team) (+ (current-time) (if (> (bf-city-spawn-near team -1) 0) (seconds 1) (seconds 0.5))))
      (set! (-> *bf-spawn-x* 0) -1000000000.0)
      (set! (-> *bf-spawn-x* 1) 1000000000.0)
      )
    (when (and (!= (-> *bf* zone) BF_ZONE_SPARGUS) (>= (current-time) (-> *bf-spawn-time* team)))
      (let ((turn (bf-transport-drop-point team)))
        ;; a held control point: a base's drops come from its ship
        (when (and (>= turn 0) (not (-> *bf* points turn base?)) (= (-> *bf* points turn owner) team))
          (set! (-> *bf-drop-turn* team) -1)
          (cond
            ((> (bf-city-spawn-near team turn) 0)
             (set! (-> *bf-spawn-time* team) (+ (current-time) (seconds 1)))
             )
            (else
              (if (>= *bf-wake-kind* 0)
                  (set! (-> *bf-drop-skip* team) turn)
                  )
              (set! (-> *bf-spawn-time* team) (+ (current-time) (seconds 0.5)))
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-sky-spot ()
  "BF_CITY_SKY_SPOT, for the player's respawn from the sky (battlefront.gc `bf-sky-drop!`): a nav
   poly drawn at random around point `*bf*` sky-point (`bf-city-spawn-spot`), the one with the most
   sky over it of up to 6 (`bf-sky-height`), into sky-ground, sky-found? #t when there is one. The meshes are listed again first: after a far respawn's reset
   the list could name meshes of levels gone."
  (let ((pt (-> *bf* sky-point))
        (best 0.0)
        (spot (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        )
    (bf-ways-build)
    (set! (-> *bf* sky-found?) #f)
    ;; up to 6 polys drawn, the one with the most sky over it
    (when (and (>= pt 0) (< pt (-> *bf* point-count)))
      (dotimes (try 6)
        (when (and (< best (meters 20)) (bf-city-spawn-spot (-> *bf* points pt pos) spot BF_RESPAWN_REACH #f))
          (let ((h (bf-sky-height spot)))
            (when (or (not (-> *bf* sky-found?)) (< best h))
              (set! best h)
              (vector-copy! (-> *bf* sky-ground) spot)
              (set! (-> *bf* sky-found?) #t)
              )
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(define *bf-nan-sleeps* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0)) ;; for the tests: units put to sleep at NaN

(define *bf-bone-fixes* (new 'static 'array int32 1 0)) ;; for the tests: units whose bones were put back

(defun bf-unit-bones-at! ((u nav-enemy) (pos vector) (w float))
  "Every bone of unit U: no rotation, its place POS with W (1.0 a place, 0.0 none: vector<-cspace!
   reads a bone with w 0 as the origin, never NaN). Its joint math overwrites them the next time
   the unit is drawn."
  (dotimes (i (-> u node-list length))
    (let ((c (-> u node-list data i)))
      (when (and (nonzero? (-> c bone)) (-> c bone))
        (let ((m (-> c bone transform)))
          (matrix-identity! m)
          (vector-copy! (-> m trans) pos)
          (set! (-> m trans w) w)
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-unit-bones-bad? ((u nav-enemy))
  "#t when unit U's bullseye bone (its enemy info's bullseye-joint, the point its foes aim at:
   get-trans 3) is NaN."
  (let ((j (-> u enemy-info bullseye-joint)))
    (and (< j (-> u node-list length))
         (let ((c (-> u node-list data j)))
           (and (nonzero? (-> c bone))
                (-> c bone)
                (or (bf-nan? (-> c bone transform trans x)) (bf-nan? (-> c bone transform trans w)))
                )
           )
         )
    )
  )

(defconstant BF_UNDER_CITY (meters -100)) ;; a unit lower than this fell through the city

(defun bf-city-land! ((u nav-enemy) (floor float) (collide collide-spec))
  "Falling unit U (exit-transport) passed FLOOR, its landing's height, with nothing under it: Jak 2's
   city, ported, has nav meshes where its scenery's collision is missing, and a robotguard or a
   spider falling there never touched ground, the only way out of its fall (spydroid.gc
   exit-transport), fell 6 km and kept its side's place (the author's report of stuck units,
   round 45). Put on FLOOR, still, its collision COLLIDE back, and walking ('active, as
   `bf-city-robot-free` sends it)."
  (set! (-> u root trans y) floor)
  (vector-reset! (-> u root transv))
  (set! (-> u root root-prim prim-core collide-with) collide)
  (go-process u (method-of-object u active))
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-rescue! ((u nav-enemy))
  "Unit U fell under the city in its way out of a ship or the sky (exit-transport), which no sleep
   takes it out of: back onto the floor of the nav poly of its mesh nearest across (`bf-city-floor`)
   and landed there (`bf-city-land!`). A robotguard put back to sleep there each frame stayed listed
   awake, 7368 times in a run (round 45). Returns #t when put back."
  (let ((mesh (if (and (nonzero? (-> u nav)) (-> u nav)) (-> u nav state mesh))))
    (when mesh
      (let ((at (vector-copy! (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector) (-> u root trans)))
            (c (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
            )
        (if (bf-nan? (-> at x))
            (vector-copy! at (the-as vector (-> mesh bounds)))
            )
        (set! (-> at y) (-> mesh bounds y))
        (let ((poly (nav-mesh-method-10 mesh at at (the-as nav-poly #f))))
          (when poly
            (poly-centroid mesh poly c)
            (set! (-> c y) (bf-city-floor c (-> c y)))
            (move-to-point! (-> u root) c)
            (bf-city-land! u (-> c y) (if (zero? (-> u root root-prim prim-core collide-with))
                                          (collide-spec backgnd)
                                          (-> u root root-prim prim-core collide-with)
                                          )
                           )
            #t
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )

(defun bf-city-nan-sweep ()
  "Every frame of the fight: each unit of the battle awake whose place, velocity or turn is not a
   number, or that fell under the city (lower than BF_UNDER_CITY: through a floor, which has no
   underside, round 45), goes back to its pool (`bf-transport-sleep`), its place free for the next one (round 32). The
   stock unit code was written against the player alone, and in unit against unit fights it made a
   unit's place NaN now and then: a jetpack guard's turn went NaN (`bf-hover-turn-fix!` mends it
   since), so did its bones and its shots, and each guard such a shot knocked flew off at NaN. Such a unit never died, kept its side's place (its side stopped
   coming down at the points: 32 units of 80 in 7 minutes, scenario 60), and every unit that took
   it as its foe chased or shot at NaN and became NaN in turn. Its bones keep NaN until it is drawn
   again, awake elsewhere too, and the jetpack guards aim at a foe's bullseye bone (flying-turret.gc
   update-focus, get-trans 3): asleep, its bones are cleared (`bf-unit-bones-at!`); awake, a unit
   whose bullseye bone is NaN gets its bones on its place (4 jetpacks of 6 NaN
   units came from one guard woken with NaN bones, scenario 60). Returns nothing; logs each one."
  (let ((te *traffic-engine*)
        (bad (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'uint64 16))
        (n 0)
        )
    (when (and te (nonzero? te))
      (dotimes (ti 2)
        (let ((tr (-> te tracker-array ti)))
          (dotimes (i (-> tr active-object-count))
            (let ((p (handle->process (-> tr active-object-list i))))
              (when (and p (< n 16) (type? p nav-enemy) (>= (bf-unit-team p) 0))
                (let ((u (the-as nav-enemy p)))
                  (cond
                    ((or (bf-nan? (-> u root trans x)) (bf-nan? (-> u root trans y)) (bf-nan? (-> u root trans z))
                         (bf-nan? (-> u root transv x)) (bf-nan? (-> u root transv z)) (bf-nan? (-> u root quat x))
                         (< (-> u root trans y) BF_UNDER_CITY)
                         )
                     (set! (-> bad n) (the-as uint (-> tr active-object-list i)))
                     (+! n 1)
                     )
                    ((bf-unit-bones-bad? u)
                     (bf-unit-bones-at! u (-> u root trans) 1.0)
                     (+! (-> *bf-bone-fixes* 0) 1)
                     )
                    )
                  )
                )
              )
            )
          )
        )
      ;; put to sleep once the lists are read: a sleep takes the unit out of its list; one under the
      ;; city on its way out of a ship or the sky, which no sleep takes out of it, put back on the
      ;; ground instead (`bf-city-rescue!`)
      (dotimes (k n)
        (let ((p (handle->process (the-as handle (-> bad k)))))
          (when (and p (-> p next-state) (= (-> p next-state name) 'exit-transport)
                     (not (bf-nan? (-> (the-as nav-enemy p) root trans y)))
                     (bf-city-rescue! (the-as nav-enemy p))
                     )
            (format 0 "battlefront: unit ~D (~A) under the city in exit-transport, put back on the ground~%" (-> p pid) (-> p type symbol))
            (set! p #f)
            )
          (when p
            (format 0 "battlefront: unit ~D (~A) at NaN or under the city in ~A, put back to sleep~%" (-> p pid) (-> p type symbol)
                    (if (-> p next-state) (-> p next-state name) '-)
                    )
            (bf-unit-bones-at! (the-as nav-enemy p) *null-vector* 0.0)
            (bf-transport-sleep p)
            (+! (-> *bf-nan-sleeps* 0) 1)
            )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-command ((cmd int))
  "`*bf-city-hook*`. CMD: BF_CITY_PREPARE once the zone is loaded, BF_CITY_UPDATE every frame of
   the fight, BF_CITY_RESET when the battle ends. The unit pools are not rebuilt here: the director
   respawns the player with `initialize!` 'life at both ends of a battle (battlefront.gc), which
   rebuilds them the way a death does."
  (cond
    ((= cmd BF_CITY_SKY_SPOT)
     (bf-city-sky-spot)
     )
    ((= cmd BF_CITY_PREPARE)
     (bf-city-restore-hatred)
     (bf-city-ships-down)
     (bf-city-sleep-all)
     )
    ((= cmd BF_CITY_UPDATE)
     (bf-city-nan-sweep)
     (bf-city-apply-hatred)
     (when (time-elapsed? (-> *bf-city-saved* retarget-time) (seconds 0.5))
       (set-time! (-> *bf-city-saved* retarget-time))
       (bf-city-retarget)
       (bf-city-steer)
       )
     (bf-march-apply)
     (bf-city-sky-tick)
     (bf-city-dots)
     (bf-city-draw-cap)
     ;; a death reset (ctywide activates again) or a task change restores the stock faction
     ;; state: apply the battle's every 2 seconds
     (when (and *cty-faction-manager*
                (nonzero? *cty-faction-manager*)
                (time-elapsed? (-> *bf-city-saved* faction-time) (seconds 2))
                )
       (set-time! (-> *bf-city-saved* faction-time))
       (cty-faction-evaluate-commands *bf-faction-commands*)
       ;; the lift to the Freedom League's headquarters stays still (elevator.gc 'go-dormant: only
       ;; a 'trigger wakes it); a death reset spawns it again, so sent each time
       (let ((lift (process-by-ename "cty-elevator-2")))
         (if lift
             (send-event lift 'go-dormant)
             )
         )
       )
     ;; the troop transports, the units from the edge, the force fields: a look twice a second
     (when (time-elapsed? (-> *bf-city-saved* reinforce-time) (seconds 0.5))
       (set-time! (-> *bf-city-saved* reinforce-time))
       (bf-city-transports)
       (bf-city-spawn-tick)
       (bf-city-edge-spawn)
       (bf-city-fields-up)
       )
     )
    ((= cmd BF_CITY_FREE_NAVS)
     (bf-city-free-navs)
     )
    ((= cmd BF_CITY_RESET)
     (bf-city-restore-hatred)
     (bf-city-ships-down)
     (bf-city-fields-down)
     )
    )
  (none)
  )

(defun bf-city-throw-grenade ((from vector) (to vector))
  "`*bf-city-grenade*`: the player throws a guard grenade from FROM onto TO, the projectile and arc
   of the grenade guards (guard-grenade.gc crimson-guard-method-264). Jak owns it and it skips him;
   with no charge it bursts where it lands, BF_GRENADE_BLAST wide (the AI grenadiers keep 4 m)."
  (let ((traj (new 'stack-no-clear 'traj3d-params)))
    (vector-copy! (-> traj src) from)
    (vector-copy! (-> traj dest) to)
    (set! (-> traj initial-tilt) 8192.0)
    (set! (-> traj gravity) 184320.0)
    (when (traj3d-calc-initial-velocity-using-tilt traj)
      (let ((params (new 'stack-no-clear 'projectile-init-by-other-params)))
        (set! (-> params ent) (-> *target* entity))
        (set! (-> params charge) 0.0)
        (set! (-> params options) (projectile-options))
        (vector-copy! (-> params pos) from)
        (vector-copy! (-> params vel) (-> traj initial-velocity))
        (set! (-> params notify-handle) (the-as handle #f))
        (set! (-> params owner-handle) (process->handle *target*))
        (set! (-> params target-handle) (the-as handle #f))
        (set! (-> params target-pos quad) (the-as uint128 0))
        (set! (-> params ignore-handle) (process->handle *target*))
        (let* ((info *game-info*)
               (id (+ (-> info attack-id) 1))
               )
          (set! (-> info attack-id) id)
          (set! (-> params attack-id) id)
          )
        (set! (-> params timeout) (seconds 4))
        ;; its blast twice the stock 4 m across (round 44, the author's wish: twice its circumference)
        (let ((proj (spawn-projectile vehicle-grenade-deflect params *target* *default-dead-pool*)))
          (if proj
              (set! (-> (the-as vehicle-grenade (ppointer->process proj)) blast-radius) BF_GRENADE_BLAST)
              )
          )
        )
      )
    )
  (none)
  )

;; install the hooks at every link of CWI (the previous values pointed into the previous link)
(set! *bf-city-hook* bf-city-command)
(set! *bf-city-grenade* bf-city-throw-grenade)
